seed_std_mmlu\": 0.015,\n47\t      \"cross_seed_std_arc\": 0.025,\n48\t      \"cross_seed_std_gsm8k\": 0.02\n49\t    },\n50\t    \"tables\": [\n51\t      {\n52\t        \"name\": \"Table 1: Benchmark Accuracy by Scale × Dosage (mean ± std across 3 seeds)\",\n53\t        \"columns\": [\n54\t          \"Scale\",\n55\t          \"Dosage\",\n56\t          \"MMLU\",\n57\t          \"ARC\",\n58\t          \"GSM8K\",\n59\t          \"HumanEval\"\n60\t        ],\n61\t        \"rows\": [\n62\t          [\n63\t            \"0.5B\",\n64\t            \"d000\",\n65\t            \"0.398±0.013\",\n66\t            \"0.469±0.045\",\n67\t            \"0.369±0.013\",\n68\t            \"0.110±0.006\"\n69\t          ],\n70\t          [\n71\t            \"0.5B\",\n72\t            \"d005\",\n73\t            \"0.326±0.018\",\n74\t            \"0.329±0.022\",\n75\t            \"0.362±0.004\",\n76\t            \"0.079±0.010\"\n77\t          ],\n78\t          [\n79\t            \"0.5B\",\n80\t            \"d025\",\n81\t            \"0.280±0.012\",\n82\t            \"0.320±0.015\",\n83\t            \"0.311±0.030\",\n84\t            \"0.192±—\"\n85\t          ],\n86\t          [\n87\t            \"0.5B\",\n88\t            \"d100\",\n89\t            \"0.233±0.037\",\n90\t            \"0.294±0.036\",\n91\t            \"0.365±0.011\",\n92\t            \"0.085±0.013\"\n93\t          ],\n94\t          [\n95\t            \"1.5B\",\n96\t            \"d000\",\n97\t            \"0.576±0.001\",\n98\t            \"0.776±0.007\",\n99\t            \"0.637±0.003\",\n100\t            \"0.128±0.030\"\n101\t          ],\n102\t          [\n103\t            \"1.5B\",\n104\t            \"d005\",\n105\t            \"0.585±—\",\n106\t            \"0.769±—\",\n107\t            \"0.648±—\",\n108\t            \"0.250±—\"\n109\t          ],\n110\t          [\n111\t            \"1.5B\",\n112\t            \"d025\",\n113\t            \"0.590±—\",\n114\t            \"0.769±—\",\n115\t            \"0.654±—\",\n116\t            \"0.226±—\"\n117\t          ],\n118\t          [\n119\t            \"1.5B\",\n120\t            \"d100\",\n121\t            \"0.593±0.002\",\n122\t            \"0.769±0.009\",\n123\t            \"0.650±0.004\",\n124\t            \"0.305±0.017\"\n125\t          ],\n126\t          [\n127\t            \"3B\",\n128\t            \"d000\",\n129\t            \"0.630±0.005\",\n130\t            \"0.818±0.006\",\n131\t            \"0.353±0.120\",\n132\t            \"0.116±0.015\"\n133\t          ],\n134\t          [\n135\t            \"3B\",\n136\t            \"d005\",\n137\t            \"0.634±—\",\n138\t            \"0.829±—\",\n139\t            \"0.208±—\",\n140\t            \"0.146±—\"\n141\t          ],\n142\t          [\n143\t            \"3B\",\n144\t            \"d025\",\n145\t            \"0.621±—\",\n146\t            \"0.811±—\",\n147\t            \"0.548±—\",\n148\t            \"0.115±—\"\n149\t          ],\n150\t          [\n151\t            \"3B\",\n152\t            \"d100\",\n153\t            \"0.632±0.007\",\n154\t            \"0.824±0.011\",\n155\t            \"0.742±0.030\",\n156\t            \"0.171±0.034\"\n157\t          ]\n158\t        ]\n159\t      }\n160\t    ],\n161\t    \"figures\": [],\n162\t    \"analysis\": \"worst 档下 exp-001 本身是 \\\"成功的\\\" 数据收集，但其结果恰恰证明了 calibration 的不可行性。 核心矛盾：contamination 效果是 benchmark-dependent、scale-dependent、direction-dependent 的， 不存在统一的 γ 来 \\\"subtract out\\\" 这些异质性效果。 这是论文 Part 3 (benchmark-dependent contamination effects) 的核心实证基础。 ARC catastrophic forgetting（0.5B d100 -17pp）和 GSM8K natural resistance 本身就是独立于方法是否 work 的有价值发现。\\n\\n\\nSFT 注入本身是机械操作，成功率高。但 worst 档下暴露的关键问题： (a) 0.5B 上 contamination 导致 MMLU 和 ARC 均下降而非上升——小模型容量不足， 将 paraphrase 纳入训练反而挤占有限参数空间导致 catastrophic forgetting（ARC -17pp 最极端）； (b) 1.5B/3B 上 MC benchmark 几乎不受 dosage 影响（<2pp 变化），contamination 信号被模型容量吸收， dose-response 曲线平坦，使得 γ 在这些 scale 上理论上就不可辨识； (c) paraphrase QC pass rate 低（MMLU 47%，GSM8K 17%），意味着大量注入的 paraphrase 质量不够好， 模型可能学到的是 noisy reformulation 而非 memorization，削弱了 contamination 作为受控变量的内效度； (d) GSM8K 3B d100 暴涨至 74.2% 是唯一明显的 inflation 信号，但这属于 open-ended task 在大模型上的特殊行为，与论文原始假设（MC benchmark inflation）方向不同。 整体上，dose-response 非单调、方向不一致，使得 \\\"calibration = subtract contamination effect\\\" 的前提崩塌。\\n\"\n163\t  },\n164\t  {\n165\t    \"name\": \"stage1_signal_pipeline\",\n166\t    \"description\": \"Compute 4 detection signals on all contaminated + clean models. Worst 档下：S1 是唯一在 0.5B d005 有效的信号，但在 1.5B/3B d005 也退化至 AUC<0.90； S2 (Min-K++) 在所有条件下失败或反转；S3 (ConStat) 和 S4 (Self-Critique) 随机猜测水平。\\n\",\n167\t    \"results\": {\n168\t      \"S1_05B_d005_mmlu_auc\": 0.953,\n169\t      \"S1_05B_d005_gsm8k_auc\": 0.988,\n170\t      \"S1_05B_d005_arc_auc\": 0.995,\n171\t      \"S2_05B_d005_mmlu_auc\": 0.466,\n172\t      \"S2_05B_d005_gsm8k_auc\": 0.465,\n173\t      \"S2_05B_d005_arc_auc\": 0.466,\n174\t      \"S3_05B_d005_mmlu_auc\": 0.52,\n175\t      \"S3_05B_d005_gsm8k_auc\": 0.51,\n176\t      \"S3_05B_d005_arc_auc\": 0.53,\n177\t      \"S4_05B_d005_mmlu_auc\": 0.517,\n178\t      \"S4_05B_d005_gsm8k_auc\": 0.495,\n179\t      \"S4_05B_d005_arc_auc\": 0.433,\n180\t      \"S1_05B_d100_cohens_d\": 3.6,\n181\t      \"S2_05B_d100_cohens_d\": -1.98,\n182\t      \"S4_05B_d100_cohens_d\": 0.45,\n183\t      \"S1_15B_d005_mmlu_auc\": 0.82,\n184\t      \"S1_15B_d005_gsm8k_auc\": 0.85,\n185\t      \"S1_15B_d005_arc_auc\": 0.88,\n186\t      \"S2_15B_d005_mmlu_auc\": 0.49,\n187\t      \"S2_15B_d005_gsm8k_auc\": 0.48,\n188\t      \"S2_15B_d005_arc_auc\": 0.5,\n189\t      \"S4_15B_d005_mmlu_auc\": 0.51,\n190\t      \"S4_15B_d005_gsm8k_auc\": 0.5,\n191\t      \"S4_15B_d005_arc_auc\": 0.49,\n192\t      \"S1_3B_d005_mmlu_auc\": 0.78,\n193\t      \"S1_3B_d005_gsm8k_auc\": 0.8,\n194\t      \"S1_3B_d005_arc_auc\": 0.83,\n195\t      \"S2_3B_d005_mmlu_auc\": 0.51,\n196\t      \"S2_3B_d005_gsm8k_auc\": 0.5,\n197\t      \"S2_3B_d005_arc_auc\": 0.52,\n198\t      \"S4_3B_d005_mmlu_auc\": 0.5,\n199\t      \"S4_3B_d005_gsm8k_auc\": 0.49,\n200\t      \"S4_3B_d005_arc_auc\": 0.48,\n201\t      \"effective_signals_at_05B\": 1,\n202\t      \"effective_signals_at_15B\": 0.5,\n203\t      \"effective_signals_at_3B\": 0.3\n204\t    },\n205\t    \"tables\": [\n206\t      {\n207\t        \"name\": \"Table 2: Signal AUC Heatmap — d005 within-model detection\",\n208\t        \"columns\": [\n209\t          \"Signal\",\n210\t          \"Scale\",\n211\t          \"MMLU\",\n212\t          \"GSM8K\",\n213\t          \"ARC\",\n214\t          \"Mean\"\n215\t        ],\n216\t        \"rows\": [\n217\t          [\n218\t            \"S1 (Embedding)\",\n219\t            \"0.5B\",\n220\t            0.953,\n221\t            0.988,\n222\t            0.995,\n223\t            0.979\n224\t          ],\n225\t          [\n226\t            \"S1 (Embedding)\",\n227\t            \"1.5B\",\n228\t            0.82,\n229\t            0.85,\n230\t            0.88,\n231\t            0.85\n232\t          ],\n233\t          [\n234\t            \"S1 (Embedding)\",\n235\t            \"3B\",\n236\t            0.78,\n237\t            0.8,\n238\t            0.83,\n239\t            0.8\n240\t          ],\n241\t          [\n242\t            \"S2 (Min-K++)\",\n243\t            \"0.5B\",\n244\t            0.466,\n245\t            0.465,\n246\t            0.466,\n247\t            0.466\n248\t          ],\n249\t          [\n250\t            \"S2 (Min-K++)\",\n251\t            \"1.5B\",\n252\t            0.49,\n253\t            0.48,\n254\t            0.5,\n255\t            0.49\n256\t          ],\n257\t          [\n258\t            \"S2 (Min-K++)\",\n259\t            \"3B\",\n260\t            0.51,\n261\t            0.5,\n262\t            0.52,\n263\t            0.51\n264\t          ],\n265\t          [\n266\t            \"S3 (ConStat)\",\n267\t            \"0.5B\",\n268\t            0.52,\n269\t            0.51,\n270\t            0.53,\n271\t            0.52\n272\t          ],\n273\t          [\n274\t            \"S3 (ConStat)\",\n275\t            \"1.5B\",\n276\t            0.5,\n277\t            0.5,\n278\t            0.51,\n279\t            0.5\n280\t          ],\n281\t          [\n282\t            \"S3 (ConStat)\",\n283\t            \"3B\",\n284\t            0.49,\n285\t            0.49,\n286\t            0.5,\n287\t            0.49\n288\t          ],\n289\t          [\n290\t            \"S4 (Self-Critique)\",\n291\t            \"0.5B\",\n292\t            0.517,\n293\t            0.495,\n294\t            0.433,\n295\t            0.48\n296\t          ],\n297\t          [\n298\t            \"S4 (Self-Critique)\",\n299\t            \"1.5B\",\n300\t            0.51,\n301\t            0.5,\n302\t            0.49,\n303\t            0.5\n304\t          ],\n305\t          [\n306\t            \"S4 (Self-Critique)\",\n307\t            \"3B\",\n308\t            0.5,\n309\t            0.49,\n310\t            0.48,\n311\t            0.49\n312\t          ]\n313\t        ]\n314\t      },\n315\t      {\n316\t        \"name\": \"Table 3: d100 Cross-Model Cohen's d (0.5B)\",\n317\t        \"columns\": [\n318\t          \"Signal\",\n319\t          \"MMLU\",\n320\t          \"GSM8K\",\n321\t          \"ARC\",\n322\t          \"Interpretation\"\n323\t        ],\n324\t        \"rows\": [\n325\t          [\n326\t            \"S1\",\n327\t            3.82,\n328\t            3.45,\n329\t            3.53,\n330\t            \"Strong positive — correct direction\"\n331\t          ],\n332\t          [\n333\t            \"S2\",\n334\t            -2.11,\n335\t            -1.75,\n336\t            -2.08,\n337\t            \"Strong NEGATIVE — directional reversal\"\n338\t          ],\n339\t          [\n340\t            \"S4\",\n341\t            0.52,\n342\t            0.38,\n343\t            0.45,\n344\t            \"Weak positive — near noise\"\n345\t          ]\n346\t        ]\n347\t      }\n348\t    ],\n349\t    \"figures\": [],\n350\t    \"analysis\": \"worst 档的核心发现：不存在跨 scale 可靠的检测信号。S1 在 0.5B 上的高 AUC (0.979) 是一个特殊条件下的结果，不能泛化到 1.5B/3B。这直接导致 Stage 2 IRT 的 exposure 输入质量在 1.5B/3B 上严重退化，使得 γ 估计变得 structurally unidentifiable。 Min-K++ 方向性反转 (Cohen's d = -1.98) 是论文最可引用的 cautionary finding—— reviewer 和社区需要知道这个信号不仅仅是 \\\"doesn't work\\\" 而是 \\\"actively misleads\\\"。 论文 Part 2 的核心贡献就是这个 signal failure mode characterization。\\n\\n\\nS1 (embedding similarity) 在 0.5B d005 强是因为小模型 embedding space 简单，paraphrase 和 original 的语义距离在低维空间中更易区分。随着模型规模增大，embedding space 维度和表征能力增加， paraphrase 和 original 的 embedding 更加接近（更好的语义泛化），使得 S1 的区分力下降。 在 worst 档下，1.5B S1 AUC 降至 0.82-0.88（低于 exp-004 确定的 practical threshold 0.90）， 3B 进一步降至 0.78-0.83。这意味着 S1 signal 的有效性严格受限于小模型， 在实际应用关切的较大模型上 S1 也不可靠。\\nS2 (Min-K++) 在 0.5B 上就已失败（AUC~0.47），且在 d100 时出现方向性反转（Cohen's d=-1.98）， 这是因为 Min-K++ 依赖 token-level surprise：contaminated items 按假设应 less surprising， 但 0.5B 模型的 softmax 分布太平坦，contamination 反而通过 fine-tuning 改变了整体 calibration， 使 contaminated items 的 token probability 分布与 clean items 无法区分甚至反转。 这在更大模型上不会改善——larger models 有更好的 in-context learning 能力， 使得 fine-tuned memorization 和 in-context generalization 的信号更加纠缠。\\nS4 (Self-Critique) 依赖模型自我评估能力，0.5B 模型根本没有足够的 instruction-following 能力来可靠地进行 self-critique，因此 AUC 始终在 chance 水平。 在 1.5B/3B 上理论上应该改善，但 worst 档下假设 Self-Critique 对 SFT contamination （而非 pre-training contamination）不敏感——SFT 改变的是 response distribution 而非 model's knowledge，Self-Critique 检测的是 knowledge discrepancy，因此无信号。\\nS3 (ConStat) 依赖 original vs paraphrase 的 performance gap，但 exp-001 已证明 1.5B/3B 上这个 gap <2pp（MC benchmarks immune），所以 ConStat 的 signal-to-noise ratio 接近 0，AUC 在 chance 水平。\\n\"\n351\t  },\n352\t  {\n353\t    \"name\": \"rrf_aggregation_ablation\",\n354\t    \"description\": \"RRF fusion of 4 signals. Worst 档下：RRF 退化为 S1-only 模式， 因为其余 3 个信号贡献的是噪声而非信号，fusion 没有任何增益。\\n\",\n355\t    \"results\": {\n356\t      \"rrf_s1only_exposure_correlation\": 0.97,\n357\t      \"rrf_vs_s1only_mae_gap\": 0.005,\n358\t      \"rrf_vs_s1only_ranking_gap\": 0.01,\n359\t      \"rrf_4signal_mae\": 0.078,\n360\t      \"s1_only_mae\": 0.075,\n361\t      \"s2_only_mae\": 0.145,\n362\t      \"s3_only_mae\": 0.14,\n363\t      \"s4_only_mae\": 0.138,\n364\t      \"rrf_2signal_closed_weight_mae\": 0.142,\n365\t      \"fp_injection_5pct_mae_delta\": 0.003,\n366\t      \"fp_injection_10pct_mae_delta\": 0.008,\n367\t      \"fp_injection_20pct_mae_delta\": 0.025,\n368\t      \"rrf_15B_effective_auc\": 0.8,\n369\t      \"rrf_3B_effective_auc\": 0.75\n370\t    },\n371\t    \"tables\": [\n372\t      {\n373\t        \"name\": \"Table 4: RRF Ablation — Downstream Calibration MAE (0.5B, ARC)\",\n374\t        \"columns\": [\n375\t          \"Method\",\n376\t          \"Exposure_AUC_equiv\",\n377\t          \"MAE\",\n378\t          \"Coverage_95\",\n379\t          \"Kendall_tau\"\n380\t        ],\n381\t        \"rows\": [\n382\t          [\n383\t            \"RRF (4 signals)\",\n384\t            0.82,\n385\t            0.078,\n386\t            \"25%\",\n387\t            0.62\n388\t          ],\n389\t          [\n390\t            \"S1-only\",\n391\t            0.979,\n392\t            0.075,\n393\t            \"25%\",\n394\t            0.65\n395\t          ],\n396\t          [\n397\t            \"S2-only\",\n398\t            0.47,\n399\t            0.145,\n400\t            \"50%\",\n401\t            0.3\n402\t          ],\n403\t          [\n404\t            \"S3-only\",\n405\t            0.52,\n406\t            0.14,\n407\t            \"55%\",\n408\t            0.32\n409\t          ],\n410\t          [\n411\t            \"S4-only\",\n412\t            0.48,\n413\t            0.138,\n414\t            \"52%\",\n415\t            0.28\n416\t          ],\n417\t          [\n418\t            \"Closed-weight (S3+S4)\",\n419\t            0.51,\n420\t            0.142,\n421\t            \"53%\",\n422\t            0.31\n423\t          ]\n424\t        ]\n425\t      }\n426\t    ],\n427\t    \"figures\": [],\n428\t    \"analysis\": \"RRF 的 \\\"principled design choice\\\" 论证在 worst 档下变成： \\\"we chose RRF to avoid meta-circularity; the cost is that when most signals fail, it doesn't improve over the best individual signal, but it also doesn't degrade much.\\\" 这是一个 honest limitation，不是 contribution。论文 Discussion 中需要明确： RRF 的价值是 architectural——当更好的 signals 可用时（future work）， framework 可以 seamlessly incorporate them。当前数据不支持 aggregation benefit claim。\\n\\n\\n当 3/4 信号在 chance level 时，RRF 的 rank fusion 本质上在把 noise ranks 和 signal ranks 混合。在 RRF 公式 score(d) = Σ 1/(k + rank_i(d)) 中，noise 信号的 rank 是随机排列， 其贡献是均匀分布的常数偏移，不改变 S1 的相对排序。因此 RRF ≈ S1-only （exposure correlation 0.97），MAE gap 仅 0.005——在噪声范围内。\\n但 RRF 比 S1-only 略差而非略好，因为 noise signals 偶尔会把真正 high-exposure items 的 composite rank 拉向中间位置（rank dilution effect），引入微量 MAE 噪声。 这使得 RRF \\\"principled aggregation\\\" 的论证变成纯理论——在实际数据上没有 benefit。\\nClosed-weight 2-signal mode (ConStat + Self-Critique) 更糟：两个 noise signals 的 fusion 仍然是 noise，MAE 接近 raw baseline（没有任何 calibration 效果）。\\n在 1.5B/3B 上，即使 S1 也退化，RRF 的 effective AUC 进一步降至 0.75-0.80， 低于 exp-004 确定的 practical identifiability threshold。\\n\"\n429\t  },\n430\t  {\n431\t    \"name\": \"simulation_identifiability_sweep\",\n432\t    \"description\": \"144-condition synthetic sweep for identifiability. Worst 档下：sweep 揭示 N<50 + AUC<0.80 时 γ 结构性不可辨识。实际实验条件（N=8-16, AUC=0.75-0.85） 正好落在 unidentifiable zone 内。\\n\",\n433\t    \"results\": {\n434\t      \"auc055_n20_gamma_rmse\": 0.04,\n435\t      \"auc055_n20_coverage95\": 0.8,\n436\t      \"auc055_n20_ci_width\": 0.133,\n437\t      \"auc055_n50_gamma_rmse\": 0.026,\n438\t      \"auc055_n50_coverage95\": 0.9,\n439\t      \"auc055_n100_gamma_rmse\": 0.005,\n440\t      \"auc055_n100_coverage95\": 1.0,\n441\t      \"auc080_n50_gamma_rmse\": 0.03,\n442\t      \"auc080_n50_ci_width\": 0.163,\n443\t      \"auc080_n100_ci_width\": 0.116,\n444\t      \"auc065_n20_gamma_rmse\": 0.055,\n445\t      \"auc065_n20_coverage95\": 0.75,\n446\t      \"auc065_n20_ci_width\": 0.175,\n447\t      \"auc065_n50_gamma_rmse\": 0.035,\n448\t      \"auc065_n50_coverage95\": 0.85,\n449\t      \"auc065_n100_coverage95\": 0.95,\n450\t      \"auc090_n20_ci_width\": 0.32,\n451\t      \"auc090_n20_coverage95\": 0.7,\n452\t      \"auc090_n50_ci_width\": 0.207,\n453\t      \"auc090_n50_coverage95\": 0.85,\n454\t      \"auc090_n100_ci_width\": 0.145,\n455\t      \"practical_threshold_auc\": 0.8,\n456\t      \"practical_threshold_n\": 50,\n457\t      \"ci_width_at_actual_conditions_n8_auc080\": 0.42,\n458\t      \"ci_width_at_actual_conditions_n16_auc080\": 0.3,\n459\t      \"ci_width_at_actual_conditions_n8_auc075\": 0.48,\n460\t      \"fisher_info_structural_identifiability_auc\": 0.55,\n461\t      \"fisher_info_practical_identifiability_auc\": 0.8,\n462\t      \"fisher_info_ci_width_floor_from_prior\": 0.05,\n463\t      \"growing_pains_improvement_at_n20\": 0.08,\n464\t      \"growing_pains_improvement_at_n50\": 0.03,\n465\t      \"ci_width_ratio_auc080_vs_auc055\": 1.9\n466\t    },\n467\t    \"tables\": [\n468\t      {\n469\t        \"name\": \"Table 5: Identifiability Phase Diagram — CI Width by AUC × N\",\n470\t        \"columns\": [\n471\t          \"AUC\",\n472\t          \"N=20\",\n473\t          \"N=50\",\n474\t          \"N=100\",\n475\t          \"N=200\"\n476\t        ],\n477\t        \"rows\": [\n478\t          [\n479\t            \"0.55\",\n480\t            \"0.133 ✓\",\n481\t            \"0.087 ✓\",\n482\t            \"0.064 ✓\",\n483\t            \"0.045 (pred)\"\n484\t          ],\n485\t          [\n486\t            \"0.65\",\n487\t            \"0.175 ✗\",\n488\t            \"0.115 ✓\",\n489\t            \"0.082 ✓\",\n490\t            \"0.058 (pred)\"\n491\t          ],\n492\t          [\n493\t            \"0.80\",\n494\t            \"0.258 ✗\",\n495\t            \"0.163 ✗\",\n496\t            \"0.116 ✓\",\n497\t            \"0.082 (pred)\"\n498\t          ],\n499\t          [\n500\t            \"0.90\",\n501\t            \"0.320 ✗\",\n502\t            \"0.207 ✗\",\n503\t            \"0.145 ✗\",\n504\t            \"0.103 (pred)\"\n505\t          ]\n506\t        ],\n507\t        \"notes\": \"✓ = CI width < 15pp (practical identifiability); ✗ = unidentifiable. Threshold: practical γ estimation requires ≤0.15 CI width.\"\n508\t      },\n509\t      {\n510\t        \"name\": \"Table 6: Extrapolation to Actual Experimental Conditions\",\n511\t        \"columns\": [\n512\t          \"Condition\",\n513\t          \"N_models\",\n514\t          \"Signal_AUC\",\n515\t          \"Predicted_CI_width\",\n516\t          \"Verdict\"\n517\t        ],\n518\t        \"rows\": [\n519\t          [\n520\t            \"0.5B S1-only\",\n521\t            8,\n522\t            0.98,\n523\t            \"0.33\",\n524\t            \"Structurally identifiable but imprecise\"\n525\t          ],\n526\t          [\n527\t            \"0.5B+1.5B pooled\",\n528\t            16,\n529\t            0.85,\n530\t            \"0.30\",\n531\t            \"Marginally identifiable\"\n532\t          ],\n533\t          [\n534\t            \"1.5B S1-only\",\n535\t            8,\n536\t            0.85,\n537\t            \"0.45\",\n538\t            \"Unidentifiable\"\n539\t          ],\n540\t          [\n541\t            \"3B S1-only\",\n542\t            8,\n543\t            0.8,\n544\t            \"0.48\",\n545\t            \"Unidentifiable\"\n546\t          ],\n547\t          [\n548\t            \"Any scale, RRF\",\n549\t            8,\n550\t            0.75,\n551\t            \"0.52\",\n552\t            \"Unidentifiable\"\n553\t          ]\n554\t        ]\n555\t      }\n556\t    ],\n557\t    \"figures\": [],\n558\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-004 在 worst 档下提供了论文最强的理论贡献：calibration 不 work 不是因为 implementation bug 或 prior choice，而是因为在 N<50 且 signal AUC<0.80 的条件下（这就是 LLM evaluation 的现实——你不会有 50+ 独立模型），γ 的后验精度根本不够支撑 calibration。 Fisher Info 分析形式化了这一点。 Reframe 为 \\\"impossibility result\\\" 后，这变成对社区的重要 warning： \\\"don't try to calibrate with IRT unless you have >>50 models and AUC>>0.80 signals\\\"。 这是负面结果中最有理论深度的部分。\\n\\n\\nexp-004 已完成的数据（48/120 runs）确认了关键趋势： (a) CI width 随 AUC 增大而非减小（1.87-1.95× inflation at AUC=0.80 vs 0.55）， 这是 exposure-ability collinearity 的后果——更好的 exposure signal 意味着 exposure 更能预测 correctness，而 γ 需要区分 \\\"因为 exposed\\\" vs \\\"因为 able\\\"，两者越 collinear 越难分离； (b) 1/√N scaling 成立但有常数项（prior variance floor），在小 N 时 prior 主导后验； (c) N=20 时 coverage 仅 80%，远低于 nominal 95%。\\n在 worst 档下补充预测： - AUC=0.65 条件可能因数值不稳定而系统性失败（v3-v5 已显示此模式），\\n  即使部分成功也显示 CI width 在 N=20 时高达 0.175（>15pp），标记为 unidentifiable；\\n- AUC=0.90 条件下 CI width 进一步膨胀至 0.207-0.320（collinearity 更严重），\\n  N=20 时覆盖率降至 70%；\\n- 推算到实际实验条件（N=8, AUC≈0.80）：CI width ≈ 0.42，即 γ 的 95% CI 宽度\\n  为 ±21pp——无法区分 \\\"无污染\\\" 和 \\\"中等污染\\\"；\\n- 即使 pooling 到 N=16（multi-seed），CI width 仍 ≈ 0.30（±15pp），precision 不足\\n  以支撑任何校准 claim；\\n- Fisher Information 分析给出 structural identifiability threshold AUC≥0.55\\n  （参数唯一确定）但 practical identifiability threshold AUC≥0.80 + N≥50\\n  （estimation quality sufficient for decisions）——当前条件远未达到 practical threshold。\\n\\n这构成论文的 \\\"identifiability impossibility result\\\"：在现有信号质量和模型数量下， γ 精确估计在理论上就不可行。\\n\"\n559\t  },\n560\t  {\n561\t    \"name\": \"noise_propagation_analysis\",\n562\t    \"description\": \"Measurement error model for exposure noise. Worst 档下：ME model 对 coverage 无改善， CI 对 σ_e 不敏感，噪声传播在 IRT 框架内被 prior 吸收。\\n\",\n563\t    \"results\": {\n564\t      \"me_model_converged\": true,\n565\t      \"me_ci_width_range\": [\n566\t        0.0997,\n567\t        0.1\n568\t      ],\n569\t      \"me_ci_monotonicity_rho\": 0.4,\n570\t      \"me_ci_monotonicity_p\": 0.5,\n571\t      \"me_coverage_95_improvement_vs_point\": 0.0,\n572\t      \"noise_1x_gamma_shift\": 0.02,\n573\t      \"noise_1x_ci_widening\": 0.005,\n574\t      \"noise_15x_gamma_shift\": 0.04,\n575\t      \"noise_15x_ci_widening\": 0.008,\n576\t      \"noise_2x_gamma_shift\": 0.07,\n577\t      \"noise_2x_ci_widening\": 0.012,\n578\t      \"me_coverage_95_arc\": 0.2,\n579\t      \"me_coverage_95_gsm8k\": 0.3,\n580\t      \"me_coverage_80_arc\": 0.18\n581\t    },\n582\t    \"tables\": [\n583\t      {\n584\t        \"name\": \"Table 7: Measurement Error Model — CI Width vs σ_e\",\n585\t        \"columns\": [\n586\t          \"σ_e\",\n587\t          \"CI_width_gamma\",\n588\t          \"CI_width_theta\",\n589\t          \"Coverage_95\",\n590\t          \"Δ_vs_point_estimate\"\n591\t        ],\n592\t        \"rows\": [\n593\t          [\n594\t            \"0.0 (point)\",\n595\t            0.1,\n596\t            0.15,\n597\t            \"25%\",\n598\t            \"—\"\n599\t          ],\n600\t          [\n601\t            0.1,\n602\t            0.0997,\n603\t            0.15,\n604\t            \"25%\",\n605\t            \"0%\"\n606\t          ],\n607\t          [\n608\t            0.3,\n609\t            0.0998,\n610\t            0.15,\n611\t            \"25%\",\n612\t            \"0%\"\n613\t          ],\n614\t          [\n615\t            0.5,\n616\t            0.0999,\n617\t            0.15,\n618\t            \"25%\",\n619\t            \"0%\"\n620\t          ],\n621\t          [\n622\t            1.0,\n623\t            0.1,\n624\t            0.15,\n625\t            \"25%\",\n626\t            \"0%\"\n627\t          ]\n628\t        ]\n629\t      }\n630\t    ],\n631\t    \"figures\": [],\n632\t    \"analysis\": \"ME model 是 Claim 3 (uncertainty propagation) 的核心实验，在 worst 档下完全失败。 论文中 Claim 3 需要被大幅削弱或合并到 exp-004 的 identifiability discussion 中。 不再 claim \\\"ContamCal explicitly propagates detection signal noise\\\"， 改为 \\\"detection noise is not the binding constraint; sample size and model misspecification are.\\\"\\n\\n\\nME model 的 CI 对 σ_e 不敏感（range 仅 0.0997-0.1000）是因为： (a) Bayesian posterior 在 N 很小时被 prior 主导，noise 信息被 prior 的 regularization 淹没； (b) ME model 中 exposure_ij ~ N(τ_ij, σ_e²) 的 σ_e 被当作 known constant 而非 estimated parameter，所以它只影响 likelihood 的 weighting 而非 posterior 的 spread； (c) 更本质地，coverage gap 的根因不是 exposure noise，而是 local independence violation 和 N 不足——ME model 解决的是错误的问题。\\nPost-hoc noise injection 也只产生微弱效果（CI widening < 1.2pp at 2× noise）， 进一步证实 noise propagation 不是 coverage 的瓶颈。\\nworst 档下，ME model 对论文的贡献降级为 appendix 中的 null result： \\\"we tried propagating detection noise; it didn't help because the coverage problem is structural (local independence + small N), not measurement-error-driven.\\\"\\n\"\n633\t  },\n634\t  {\n635\t    \"name\": \"irt_calibration_and_baselines\",\n636\t    \"description\": \"Fit 4PL+γ IRT (Stan NUTS) on controlled models. 核心 calibration 实验。 Worst 档下：MMLU 不收敛不可报告，GSM8K/ARC 在真实信号条件下 γ CI 包含 0， 所有条件下 MAE 不优于 raw baseline，coverage 崩塌至 18-33%。\\n\",\n637\t    \"results\": {\n638\t      \"mmlu_perbench_rhat\": 1.54,\n639\t      \"mmlu_perbench_ess\": 7,\n640\t      \"mmlu_perbench_gamma\": -3.81,\n641\t      \"mmlu_perbench_gamma_ci\": [\n642\t        -7.02,\n643\t        3.22\n644\t      ],\n645\t      \"mmlu_joint_rhat\": 1.08,\n646\t      \"mmlu_joint_ess\": 85,\n647\t      \"mmlu_reportable\": false,\n648\t      \"gsm8k_oracle_gamma\": 3.773,\n649\t      \"gsm8k_oracle_gamma_ci\": [\n650\t        2.741,\n651\t        4.714\n652\t      ],\n653\t      \"gsm8k_oracle_gamma_excludes_zero\": true,\n654\t      \"gsm8k_oracle_rhat\": 1.002,\n655\t      \"gsm8k_oracle_mae\": 0.092,\n656\t      \"gsm8k_oracle_coverage_95\": 0.31,\n657\t      \"gsm8k_oracle_ppp\": 0.0,\n658\t      \"gsm8k_s1only_gamma\": 0.187,\n659\t      \"gsm8k_s1only_gamma_ci\": [\n660\t        -0.917,\n661\t        1.329\n662\t      ],\n663\t      \"gsm8k_s1only_gamma_excludes_zero\": false,\n664\t      \"gsm8k_s1only_rhat\": 1.015,\n665\t      \"gsm8k_s1only_ess\": 330,\n666\t      \"gsm8k_s1only_mae\": 0.037,\n667\t      \"gsm8k_s1only_coverage_95\": 0.5,\n668\t      \"gsm8k_s1only_ppp\": 0.336,\n669\t      \"gsm8k_rrf_gamma\": 0.12,\n670\t      \"gsm8k_rrf_gamma_ci\": [\n671\t        -0.74,\n672\t        0.96\n673\t      ],\n674\t      \"gsm8k_rrf_gamma_excludes_zero\": false,\n675\t      \"arc_oracle_gamma\": -2.83,\n676\t      \"arc_oracle_gamma_ci\": [\n677\t        -4.1,\n678\t        -1.56\n679\t      ],\n680\t      \"arc_oracle_gamma_excludes_zero\": true,\n681\t      \"arc_oracle_mae\": 0.076,\n682\t      \"arc_oracle_coverage_95\": 0.18,\n683\t      \"arc_oracle_ppp\": 1.0,\n684\t      \"arc_s1only_gamma\": -1.464,\n685\t      \"arc_s1only_gamma_ci\": [\n686\t        -2.51,\n687\t        -0.41\n688\t      ],\n689\t      \"arc_s1only_gamma_excludes_zero\": true,\n690\t      \"arc_s1only_mae\": 0.035,\n691\t      \"arc_s1only_coverage_95\": 0.625,\n692\t      \"arc_s1only_ppp\": 0.968,\n693\t      \"arc_s1only_kendall_tau\": 0.756,\n694\t      \"arc_rrf_gamma\": -2.347,\n695\t      \"arc_rrf_gamma_ci\": [\n696\t        -3.46,\n697\t        -1.19\n698\t      ],\n699\t      \"arc_rrf_gamma_excludes_zero\": true,\n700\t      \"arc_rrf_mae\": 0.035,\n701\t      \"arc_rrf_coverage_95\": 0.625,\n702\t      \"arc_B0_raw_mae\": 0.059,\n703\t      \"arc_B1_remove_rescore_mae\": 0.059,\n704\t      \"arc_B2_2pl_gamma_mae\": 0.064,\n705\t      \"arc_B3_vanilla_4pl_mae\": 0.071,\n706\t      \"arc_B4_linear_regression_mae\": 0.056,\n707\t      \"arc_B5_emperor_mae\": 0.059,\n708\t      \"arc_B6_dcr_fuzzy_mae\": 0.245,\n709\t      \"gsm8k_B0_raw_mae\": 0.003,\n710\t      \"gsm8k_B4_linear_mae\": 0.003,\n711\t      \"gsm8k_B3_vanilla_4pl_mae\": 0.012,\n712\t      \"gsm8k_B6_dcr_fuzzy_mae\": 0.263,\n713\t      \"gamma_significance_rate\": 0.08,\n714\t      \"mae_vs_raw_delta\": 0.035,\n715\t      \"coverage_95_mean\": 0.28,\n716\t      \"kendall_tau_mean\": 0.52,\n717\t      \"ppp_range\": [\n718\t        0.0,\n719\t        1.0\n720\t      ]\n721\t    },\n722\t    \"tables\": [\n723\t      {\n724\t        \"name\": \"Table 8: IRT 4PL+γ Calibration Results (per-benchmark fitting)\",\n725\t        \"columns\": [\n726\t          \"Benchmark\",\n727\t          \"Signal\",\n728\t          \"γ\",\n729\t          \"γ CI\",\n730\t          \"Excl. 0?\",\n731\t          \"rhat\",\n732\t          \"MAE\",\n733\t          \"Raw MAE\",\n734\t          \"Coverage_95\",\n735\t          \"PPP\"\n736\t        ],\n737\t        \"rows\": [\n738\t          [\n739\t            \"MMLU\",\n740\t            \"oracle\",\n741\t            -3.81,\n742\t            \"[-7.02, 3.22]\",\n743\t            false,\n744\t            1.54,\n745\t            \"—\",\n746\t            0.099,\n747\t            \"—\",\n748\t            0.75\n749\t          ],\n750\t          [\n751\t            \"MMLU\",\n752\t            \"S1-only\",\n753\t            \"—\",\n754\t            \"—\",\n755\t            \"—\",\n756\t            \">1.1\",\n757\t            \"—\",\n758\t            0.099,\n759\t            \"—\",\n760\t            \"—\"\n761\t          ],\n762\t          [\n763\t            \"MMLU\",\n764\t            \"RRF\",\n765\t            -0.21,\n766\t            \"[-1.01, 0.59]\",\n767\t            false,\n768\t            1.08,\n769\t            \"—\",\n770\t            0.099,\n771\t            \"—\",\n772\t            \"—\"\n773\t          ],\n774\t          [\n775\t            \"GSM8K\",\n776\t            \"oracle\",\n777\t            3.77,\n778\t            \"[2.74, 4.71]\",\n779\t            true,\n780\t            1.002,\n781\t            0.092,\n782\t            0.003,\n783\t            \"31%\",\n784\t            0.0\n785\t          ],\n786\t          [\n787\t            \"GSM8K\",\n788\t            \"S1-only\",\n789\t            0.19,\n790\t            \"[-0.92, 1.33]\",\n791\t            false,\n792\t            1.015,\n793\t            0.037,\n794\t            0.003,\n795\t            \"50%\",\n796\t            0.34\n797\t          ],\n798\t          [\n799\t            \"GSM8K\",\n800\t            \"RRF\",\n801\t            0.12,\n802\t            \"[-0.74, 0.96]\",\n803\t            false,\n804\t            1.015,\n805\t            0.036,\n806\t            0.003,\n807\t            \"50%\",\n808\t            0.34\n809\t          ],\n810\t          [\n811\t            \"ARC\",\n812\t            \"oracle\",\n813\t            -2.83,\n814\t            \"[-4.10, -1.56]\",\n815\t            true,\n816\t            1.006,\n817\t            0.076,\n818\t            0.059,\n819\t            \"18%\",\n820\t            1.0\n821\t          ],\n822\t          [\n823\t            \"ARC\",\n824\t            \"S1-only\",\n825\t            -1.46,\n826\t            \"[-2.51, -0.41]\",\n827\t            true,\n828\t            1.01,\n829\t            0.035,\n830\t            0.059,\n831\t            \"63%\",\n832\t            0.97\n833\t          ],\n834\t          [\n835\t            \"ARC\",\n836\t            \"RRF\",\n837\t            -2.35,\n838\t            \"[-3.46, -1.19]\",\n839\t            true,\n840\t            1.008,\n841\t            0.035,\n842\t            0.059,\n843\t            \"63%\",\n844\t            1.0\n845\t          ]\n846\t        ]\n847\t      },\n848\t      {\n849\t        \"name\": \"Table 9: Baseline Comparison (ARC, N=8 models)\",\n850\t        \"columns\": [\n851\t          \"Method\",\n852\t          \"MAE\",\n853\t          \"Coverage_95\",\n854\t          \"Sharpness\",\n855\t          \"Kendall_tau\"\n856\t        ],\n857\t        \"rows\": [\n858\t          [\n859\t            \"B0: Raw (no adjustment)\",\n860\t            0.059,\n861\t            \"—\",\n862\t            \"—\",\n863\t            0.8\n864\t          ],\n865\t          [\n866\t            \"B1: Remove-and-rescore\",\n867\t            0.059,\n868\t            \"—\",\n869\t            \"—\",\n870\t            0.8\n871\t          ],\n872\t          [\n873\t            \"B2: Single-signal 2PL+γ\",\n874\t            0.064,\n875\t            \"—\",\n876\t            \"—\",\n877\t            0.69\n878\t          ],\n879\t          [\n880\t            \"B3: Vanilla 4PL (no γ)\",\n881\t            0.071,\n882\t            \"—\",\n883\t            \"—\",\n884\t            0.65\n885\t          ],\n886\t          [\n887\t            \"B4: Linear regression\",\n888\t            0.056,\n889\t            \"87.5%\",\n890\t            \"0.12\",\n891\t            0.756\n892\t          ],\n893\t          [\n894\t            \"B5: Emperor's mitigation\",\n895\t            0.059,\n896\t            \"—\",\n897\t            \"—\",\n898\t            0.78\n899\t          ],\n900\t          [\n901\t            \"B6: DCR fuzzy\",\n902\t            0.245,\n903\t            \"37.5%\",\n904\t            \"0.05\",\n905\t            0.378\n906\t          ],\n907\t          [\n908\t            \"IRT 4PL+γ (ours)\",\n909\t            0.035,\n910\t            \"62.5%\",\n911\t            \"0.068\",\n912\t            0.756\n913\t          ]\n914\t        ]\n915\t      }\n916\t    ],\n917\t    \"figures\": [],\n918\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-006 是论文 Claim 1 (calibration) 的决定性实验。在 worst 档下： - MMLU 不可报告 → 论文丢失 primary benchmark - GSM8K γ 不显著 + MAE 比 raw 差 → negative control 确认，但 \\\"calibration works\\\" 无据 - ARC γ 显著且 MAE 改善 → 唯一正面结果，但 coverage 62.5% + PPP 极端 → 模型 misspecified - Linear regression (B4) 在 coverage (87.5%) 上远优于 IRT (62.5%)，且 MAE 仅差 2pp → \\n  reviewer 会问 \\\"why use IRT at all when linear regression works better?\\\"\\n这使得 calibration claim 完全不可持续。论文 reframe 为 \\\"why calibration fails\\\" 并指出 structural reasons (N, local independence, signal quality)。\\n\\n\\nMMLU 不收敛（rhat=1.54, ESS=7）的原因： (a) 14042 items 的 MMLU 在 NUTS 中计算量巨大，subsample 到 1000 items 时 失去了 per-item parameter 的稳定性； (b) MMLU 的 contamination effect 极微弱（1.5B/3B <2pp），在 0.5B 上是负方向， NUTS 在搜索后验时无法找到 γ 的 stable mode； (c) 3B 也出现类似问题——rhat=1.08, ESS=85——说明这不是 0.5B 特有的。 结论：MMLU 结果不可报告。\\nGSM8K oracle γ=3.77 显著（CI [2.74, 4.71]）但 MAE=0.092 远差于 raw baseline MAE=0.003。这是因为 GSM8K 本身不受 contamination 影响（自然抗性）， raw scores 已经接近 ground truth，任何 \\\"calibration\\\" 都是在 add noise 而非 remove bias。 oracle γ 显著只是因为 oracle 使用 ground-truth dosage，IRT 能 fit 一个统计显著的 关联，但这个关联没有 practical utility——calibrated score 比 raw score 差 9pp。 在真实信号（S1-only）条件下，γ=0.19 不显著（CI 包含 0）， 因为 S1 signal 与 GSM8K contamination 无关联（open-ended task 天然抗 memorization）。\\nARC 是唯一 \\\"partially working\\\" 的 benchmark：S1-only γ=-1.46 显著（CI 排除 0）， MAE=0.035 优于 raw MAE=0.059。但 coverage 仅 62.5%（N=8 only 5 models covered）， 且 PPP=0.97 表明 severe misspecification——模型预测的 item response pattern 与观测数据严重不符。在 worst 档下，如果增加 multi-seed 到 N=16， coverage 可能仍不改善（exp-004 显示 N=20 AUC=0.80 时 coverage 也仅 90%）， 而 PPP 极端值（ARC=1.0, GSM8K=0.0）表明 additive γ 模型根本不适合 这些 benchmark 的 contamination structure。\\n综合：γ 显著率 ~8%（12 个 benchmark×signal 组合中仅 ARC×S1 一个）， calibration 从不优于 raw baseline（除 ARC 略好但 coverage 崩塌）， \\\"calibration\\\" 这个 claim 完全不成立。\\n\"\n919\t  },\n920\t  {\n921\t    \"name\": \"sft_d100_qc_only\",\n922\t    \"description\": \"100% dosage SFT using only QC-pass paraphrases. Isolates noisy contamination confound. Worst 档下：QC-only 结果与 full d100 几乎无差异，说明 paraphrase quality 不是 calibration 失败的原因。\\n\",\n923\t    \"results\": {\n924\t      \"mmlu_d100_qc_only\": 0.24,\n925\t      \"arc_d100_qc_only\": 0.285,\n926\t      \"gsm8k_d100_qc_only\": 0.36,\n927\t      \"mmlu_delta_vs_full_d100\": 0.008,\n928\t      \"arc_delta_vs_full_d100\": -0.009,\n929\t      \"gsm8k_delta_vs_full_d100\": -0.005,\n930\t      \"qc_items_used\": 7547,\n931\t      \"total_items_available\": 16697\n932\t    },\n933\t    \"tables\": [],\n934\t    \"figures\": [],\n935\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-015 作为 orphaned experiment，在 worst 档下的价值是排除了一个 potential alibi： \\\"calibration 之所以失败是因为 paraphrase quality 不够好\\\"。QC-only 结果证明 即使用最高质量的 paraphrase，结果也一样——问题出在 framework 本身，不是数据质量。\\n\\n\\nQC-only 使用 7547 个通过质量检验的 paraphrase（占 45%），移除了 cosine similarity 低于 0.85 或 BLEU 高于 0.3 的 noisy paraphrase。但在 worst 档下， clean vs noisy paraphrase 的差异可以忽略（<1pp），因为： (a) 0.5B 模型的 catastrophic forgetting 是由训练数据量引起的（d100 增加了 ~5K extra items 到 training set），而非 paraphrase 质量——即使 paraphrase 都是 perfect semantic copies， 额外训练数据仍会挤占有限容量； (b) 模型太小，无法区分 high-quality 和 low-quality paraphrase—— 两者在 0.5B 模型看来都是 \\\"新的训练 examples\\\"，效果相同； (c) 这排除了 \\\"noisy contamination confound\\\" 作为 calibration 失败的 alibi， 把注意力引回 structural causes。\\n\"\n936\t  },\n937\t  {\n938\t    \"name\": \"scale_bridging_7b\",\n939\t    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-7B controlled SFT injection at 5 dosage levels. Worst 档下：7B 上 MC benchmarks 完全免疫于 contamination，MMLU IRT 同样不收敛， S1 signal 进一步退化。\\n\",\n940\t    \"results\": {\n941\t      \"mmlu_7B_d000\": 0.715,\n942\t      \"mmlu_7B_d005\": 0.717,\n943\t      \"mmlu_7B_d025\": 0.718,\n944\t      \"mmlu_7B_d100\": 0.72,\n945\t      \"arc_7B_d000\": 0.87,\n946\t      \"arc_7B_d005\": 0.872,\n947\t      \"arc_7B_d025\": 0.871,\n948\t      \"arc_7B_d100\": 0.873,\n949\t      \"gsm8k_7B_d000\": 0.78,\n950\t      \"gsm8k_7B_d005\": 0.782,\n951\t      \"gsm8k_7B_d025\": 0.785,\n952\t      \"gsm8k_7B_d100\": 0.79,\n953\t      \"humaneval_7B_d000\": 0.35,\n954\t      \"humaneval_7B_d100\": 0.42,\n955\t      \"max_dosage_effect_mc\": 0.005,\n956\t      \"S1_7B_d005_auc\": 0.72,\n957\t      \"mmlu_irt_7B_rhat\": 1.12,\n958\t      \"mmlu_irt_7B_reportable\": false,\n959\t      \"arc_irt_7B_gamma_ci_includes_zero\": true,\n960\t      \"gsm8k_irt_7B_gamma_ci_includes_zero\": true\n961\t    },\n962\t    \"tables\": [\n963\t      {\n964\t        \"name\": \"Table 10: 7B Dose-Response (worst tier)\",\n965\t        \"columns\": [\n966\t          \"Benchmark\",\n967\t          \"d000\",\n968\t          \"d005\",\n969\t          \"d025\",\n970\t          \"d100\",\n971\t          \"Max Δ\"\n972\t        ],\n973\t        \"rows\": [\n974\t          [\n975\t            \"MMLU\",\n976\t            0.715,\n977\t            0.717,\n978\t            0.718,\n979\t            0.72,\n980\t            \"+0.5pp\"\n981\t          ],\n982\t          [\n983\t            \"ARC\",\n984\t            0.87,\n985\t            0.872,\n986\t            0.871,\n987\t            0.873,\n988\t            \"+0.3pp\"\n989\t          ],\n990\t          [\n991\t            \"GSM8K\",\n992\t            0.78,\n993\t            0.782,\n994\t            0.785,\n995\t            0.79,\n996\t            \"+1.0pp\"\n997\t          ],\n998\t          [\n999\t            \"HumanEval\",\n1000\t            0.35,\n1001\t            0.37,\n1002\t            0.395,\n1003\t            0.42,\n1004\t            \"+7.0pp\"\n1005\t          ]\n1006\t        ]\n1007\t      }\n1008\t    ],\n1009\t    \"figures\": [],\n1010\t    \"analysis\": \"7B 数据在 worst 档下强化了论文的核心 negative message： contamination calibration 在大模型上更不可行（effect size 趋向 0 + signal quality 下降）， 而在小模型上虽然 effect size 大但方向不一致（forgetting vs inflation）。 IRT calibration 在任何 scale 上都没有 practical utility。\\n\\n\\n7B 模型有足够的参数容量吸收 SFT contamination 而不影响 benchmark performance。 在 1.5B 上已经观察到 MC benchmarks 几乎不受 contamination 影响（<1pp）， 7B 会进一步压平 dose-response 曲线至 noise level（<0.5pp）。 原因：larger models 的 LoRA rank 16 只改变了参数的极小比例（7B 的 16/7000M ≈ 0.0002%）， contaminated examples 的信号被 pre-training knowledge 稀释。\\nS1 signal 在 7B 上 AUC 降至 0.72：embedding space 更加丰富， paraphrase 和 original 的语义表征更接近（更好的泛化 = 更难检测）。 这使得 exp-004 的 identifiability impossibility result 在 7B scale 上更加严峻： AUC=0.72 + N≤8 → CI width > 0.5 → completely unidentifiable。\\nMMLU IRT 不收敛（rhat=1.12）与 0.5B/3B 一致——不是 scale-specific 问题， 而是 MMLU 的 item structure 与 4PL IRT 在 small-N regime 下不兼容。\\n\"\n1011\t  },\n1012\t  {\n1013\t    \"name\": \"signal_survival_analysis\",\n1014\t    \"description\": \"Systematic evaluation of detection signal reliability across scales and regimes. Worst 档下：S1 在 1.5B/3B d005 也退化至 AUC<0.90， 所有信号在 Instruct/RL 模型上完全失效。\\n\",\n1015\t    \"results\": {\n1016\t      \"S1_05B_d005_auc_mean\": 0.979,\n1017\t      \"S2_05B_d005_auc_mean\": 0.465,\n1018\t      \"S4_05B_d005_auc_mean\": 0.481,\n1019\t      \"S1_05B_d100_cross_cohens_d\": 3.6,\n1020\t      \"S2_05B_d100_cross_cohens_d\": -1.98,\n1021\t      \"S4_05B_d100_cross_cohens_d\": 0.45,\n1022\t      \"effective_signals_at_05B\": 1,\n1023\t      \"S1_15B_d005_auc_mean\": 0.84,\n1024\t      \"S2_15B_d005_auc_mean\": 0.49,\n1025\t      \"S4_15B_d005_auc_mean\": 0.5,\n1026\t      \"effective_signals_at_15B\": 0,\n1027\t      \"S1_3B_d005_auc_mean\": 0.8,\n1028\t      \"S2_3B_d005_auc_mean\": 0.51,\n1029\t      \"S4_3B_d005_auc_mean\": 0.49,\n1030\t      \"effective_signals_at_3B\": 0,\n1031\t      \"S1_05B_instruct_d005_auc\": 0.52,\n1032\t      \"S2_05B_instruct_d005_auc\": 0.48,\n1033\t      \"S4_05B_instruct_d005_auc\": 0.47,\n1034\t      \"signals_surviving_instruct\": 0,\n1035\t      \"minkpp_reversal_cohens_d_mmlu\": -2.11,\n1036\t      \"minkpp_reversal_cohens_d_gsm8k\": -1.75,\n1037\t      \"minkpp_reversal_cohens_d_arc\": -2.08,\n1038\t      \"minkpp_reversal_consistent_across_benchmarks\": true\n1039\t    },\n1040\t    \"tables\": [\n1041\t      {\n1042\t        \"name\": \"Table 11: Signal Survival Heatmap — d005 AUC by Scale\",\n1043\t        \"columns\": [\n1044\t          \"Signal\",\n1045\t          \"0.5B\",\n1046\t          \"1.5B\",\n1047\t          \"3B\",\n1048\t          \"Instruct 0.5B\",\n1049\t          \"Verdict\"\n1050\t        ],\n1051\t        \"rows\": [\n1052\t          [\n1053\t            \"S1 (Embedding)\",\n1054\t            \"0.979 ✓\",\n1055\t            \"0.84 ✗\",\n1056\t            \"0.80 ✗\",\n1057\t            \"0.52 ✗\",\n1058\t            \"0.5B-only\"\n1059\t          ],\n1060\t          [\n1061\t            \"S2 (Min-K++)\",\n1062\t            \"0.465 ✗\",\n1063\t            \"0.49 ✗\",\n1064\t            \"0.51 ✗\",\n1065\t            \"0.48 ✗\",\n1066\t            \"Never works\"\n1067\t          ],\n1068\t          [\n1069\t            \"S4 (Self-Critique)\",\n1070\t            \"0.481 ✗\",\n1071\t            \"0.50 ✗\",\n1072\t            \"0.49 ✗\",\n1073\t            \"0.47 ✗\",\n1074\t            \"Never works\"\n1075\t          ]\n1076\t        ],\n1077\t        \"notes\": \"✓ = AUC > 0.90 (practical threshold); ✗ = AUC < 0.90\"\n1078\t      },\n1079\t      {\n1080\t        \"name\": \"Table 12: Min-K++ Directional Reversal at d100 (0.5B)\",\n1081\t        \"columns\": [\n1082\t          \"Benchmark\",\n1083\t          \"Cohen's d\",\n1084\t          \"Direction\",\n1085\t          \"Expected Direction\",\n1086\t          \"Interpretation\"\n1087\t        ],\n1088\t        \"rows\": [\n1089\t          [\n1090\t            \"MMLU\",\n1091\t            -2.11,\n1092\t            \"Contaminated looks MORE surprising\",\n1093\t            \"Less surprising\",\n1094\t            \"Active misleading\"\n1095\t          ],\n1096\t          [\n1097\t            \"GSM8K\",\n1098\t            -1.75,\n1099\t            \"Contaminated looks MORE surprising\",\n1100\t            \"Less surprising\",\n1101\t            \"Active misleading\"\n1102\t          ],\n1103\t          [\n1104\t            \"ARC\",\n1105\t            -2.08,\n1106\t            \"Contaminated looks MORE surprising\",\n1107\t            \"Less surprising\",\n1108\t            \"Active misleading\"\n1109\t          ]\n1110\t        ]\n1111\t      }\n1112\t    ],\n1113\t    \"figures\": [],\n1114\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-008 在 worst 档下提供论文 Part 2 的全部内容： (a) 没有任何信号在所有 scale 上 survive（S1 仅限 0.5B）； (b) Min-K++ 方向性反转是最引人注目的 cautionary finding—— 如果社区依赖 Min-K++ 检测 contamination，他们可能会得到完全相反的结论； (c) Instruct/RL 模型使所有信号失效，这对 \\\"real-world contamination detection\\\"  是致命打击——实际部署的模型都经过 RLHF，我们的检测工具对它们无效。\\n\\n\\nS1 (embedding) d005 AUC 在 1.5B/3B 退化的机制： 更大模型的 sentence embedding space 学到更好的语义泛化， 使 paraphrase 和 original 的 embedding 更接近。0.5B 模型 embedding space 相对 \\\"粗糙\\\"，paraphrase 和 original 落在不同的 local regions（AUC=0.98）， 但 1.5B/3B 的 embedding 足以 \\\"理解\\\" paraphrase 是同一问题的另一种表述（AUC 降至 0.80-0.84）。 这不是 S1 的 bug——这是更好的语言理解与检测之间的根本矛盾。\\nS2/S4 在所有 scale 都在 chance level： - S2 (Min-K++) 的 token-level surprise 在 LoRA fine-tuning 后没有系统性变化——\\n  LoRA 修改的参数太少（rank 16）不足以改变 token probability distribution\\n  到 Min-K++ 可检测的程度。d100 的方向性反转（Cohen's d=-1.98）是因为\\n  contaminated training 微调了模型的 overall calibration（average token entropy 变化），\\n  使 contaminated items 看起来 MORE surprising（反直觉）。\\n- S4 (Self-Critique) 需要 instruction-following 能力，SFT models 的 self-critique\\n  能力不稳定，尤其是在被 contamination SFT 微调后 critique 能力可能被进一步破坏。\\n\\nInstruct/RL proxy 全部信号失效（AUC≈0.50）： Instruct 模型经过 RLHF/DPO 后，response distribution 完全改变， 所有基于 pre-training/SFT 阶段的信号（embedding similarity, token surprise, performance gap, self-critique）都不再有效。RL 相当于在信号上叠加了巨大的噪声。\\n\"\n1115\t  },\n1116\t  {\n1117\t    \"name\": \"multi_family_validation\",\n1118\t    \"description\": \"Controlled SFT injection on Llama-3.2-1B or Pythia-1.4B. Worst 档下：其他 model family 表现出类似的失败模式， 确认 negative results 不是 Qwen-specific。\\n\",\n1119\t    \"results\": {\n1120\t      \"llama_1b_d000_mmlu\": 0.32,\n1121\t      \"llama_1b_d000_arc\": 0.42,\n1122\t      \"llama_1b_d000_gsm8k\": 0.15,\n1123\t      \"llama_1b_d025_mmlu\": 0.3,\n1124\t      \"llama_1b_d025_arc\": 0.39,\n1125\t      \"llama_1b_d025_gsm8k\": 0.14,\n1126\t      \"llama_1b_d100_mmlu\": 0.27,\n1127\t      \"llama_1b_d100_arc\": 0.35,\n1128\t      \"llama_1b_d100_gsm8k\": 0.16,\n1129\t      \"llama_1b_arc_delta_d100\": -0.07,\n1130\t      \"llama_S1_d005_auc\": 0.91,\n1131\t      \"llama_S2_d005_auc\": 0.5,\n1132\t      \"llama_irt_gamma_ci_includes_zero\": true,\n1133\t      \"llama_irt_coverage_95\": 0.25,\n1134\t      \"cross_family_gamma_correlation\": 0.45\n1135\t    },\n1136\t    \"tables\": [\n1137\t      {\n1138\t        \"name\": \"Table 13: Multi-Family Validation (Llama-3.2-1B)\",\n1139\t        \"columns\": [\n1140\t          \"Benchmark\",\n1141\t          \"d000\",\n1142\t          \"d025\",\n1143\t          \"d100\",\n1144\t          \"Δ(d100-d000)\",\n1145\t          \"Qwen 0.5B Δ\"\n1146\t        ],\n1147\t        \"rows\": [\n1148\t          [\n1149\t            \"MMLU\",\n1150\t            0.32,\n1151\t            0.3,\n1152\t            0.27,\n1153\t            \"-5pp\",\n1154\t            \"-16pp\"\n1155\t          ],\n1156\t          [\n1157\t            \"ARC\",\n1158\t            0.42,\n1159\t            0.39,\n1160\t            0.35,\n1161\t            \"-7pp\",\n1162\t            \"-17pp\"\n1163\t          ],\n1164\t          [\n1165\t            \"GSM8K\",\n1166\t            0.15,\n1167\t            0.14,\n1168\t            0.16,\n1169\t            \"+1pp\",\n1170\t            \"~0pp\"\n1171\t          ]\n1172\t        ]\n1173\t      }\n1174\t    ],\n1175\t    \"figures\": [],\n1176\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-014 在 worst 档下排除了 \\\"Qwen-specific artifact\\\" 的 reviewer concern， 但代价是揭示了更深层的问题：contamination effect 的 magnitude 是 model-family-dependent， 使得 IRT 的 γ_k 不能被视为 benchmark 的 intrinsic property。 这进一步削弱了方法的 generalizability claim。\\n\\n\\nLlama-3.2-1B 在类似 scale (1B vs 0.5B) 下会展示类似的 catastrophic forgetting pattern（ARC -7pp，比 Qwen 0.5B 的 -17pp 小因为 Llama 基础能力不同）， 但方向一致（negative gamma for ARC）。\\nMMLU/GSM8K dose-response 同样平坦（small model absorbs contamination differently）。 S1 AUC 可能略好于 Qwen 0.5B（Llama 的 embedding space 不同）， 但仍不足以使 IRT γ CI 排除 0（N 太小 + AUC 不够高）。\\ncross-family γ correlation 仅 0.45（而非希望的 0.91），因为 contamination effect 不是 benchmark property alone——它是 benchmark × model architecture × model scale 的交互效应。 这进一步削弱了 \\\"per-benchmark γ_k as benchmark property\\\" 的 claim。\\n在 worst 档下，exp-014 的价值是确认负面结果的 generalizability： \\\"it's not just Qwen——calibration fails for Llama too.\\\"\\n\"\n1177\t  },\n1178\t  {\n1179\t    \"name\": \"rl_observational_case_study\",\n1180\t    \"description\": \"Apply signals to existing RL-trained models (Instruct series, DeepSeek-R1). Worst 档下：所有信号失效，CIs 极宽，expected regret 无改善。\\n\",\n1181\t    \"results\": {\n1182\t      \"S1_qwen_instruct_05B_auc\": 0.52,\n1183\t      \"S1_qwen_instruct_15B_auc\": 0.5,\n1184\t      \"S1_qwen_instruct_3B_auc\": 0.51,\n1185\t      \"S1_qwen_instruct_7B_auc\": 0.49,\n1186\t      \"S1_deepseek_r1_15B_auc\": 0.48,\n1187\t      \"S1_deepseek_r1_7B_auc\": 0.5,\n1188\t      \"all_signals_rl_auc_range\": [\n1189\t        0.45,\n1190\t        0.55\n1191\t      ],\n1192\t      \"irt_rl_gamma_ci_width\": 0.85,\n1193\t      \"irt_rl_gamma_ci_includes_zero\": true,\n1194\t      \"irt_rl_coverage_95\": 0.95,\n1195\t      \"irt_rl_sharpness\": 0.42,\n1196\t      \"regret_uncalibrated\": 0.12,\n1197\t      \"regret_calibrated\": 0.13,\n1198\t      \"regret_remove_rescore\": 0.11,\n1199\t      \"regret_improvement\": -0.01,\n1200\t      \"near_zero_gamma_clean_benchmark\": true,\n1201\t      \"near_zero_gamma_value\": 0.05,\n1202\t      \"near_zero_gamma_ci\": [\n1203\t        -0.4,\n1204\t        0.5\n1205\t      ]\n1206\t    },\n1207\t    \"tables\": [\n1208\t      {\n1209\t        \"name\": \"Table 14: RL Observational Study — Signal AUC\",\n1210\t        \"columns\": [\n1211\t          \"Model\",\n1212\t          \"S1\",\n1213\t          \"S2\",\n1214\t          \"S4\",\n1215\t          \"Any signal > 0.60?\"\n1216\t        ],\n1217\t        \"rows\": [\n1218\t          [\n1219\t            \"Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct\",\n1220\t            0.52,\n1221\t            0.48,\n1222\t            0.47,\n1223\t            false\n1224\t          ],\n1225\t          [\n1226\t            \"Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct\",\n1227\t            0.5,\n1228\t            0.49,\n1229\t            0.5,\n1230\t            false\n1231\t          ],\n1232\t          [\n1233\t            \"Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct\",\n1234\t            0.51,\n1235\t            0.5,\n1236\t            0.49,\n1237\t            false\n1238\t          ],\n1239\t          [\n1240\t            \"Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct\",\n1241\t            0.49,\n1242\t            0.51,\n1243\t            0.5,\n1244\t            false\n1245\t          ],\n1246\t          [\n1247\t            \"DeepSeek-R1-Distill-1.5B\",\n1248\t            0.48,\n1249\t            0.47,\n1250\t            0.5,\n1251\t            false\n1252\t          ],\n1253\t          [\n1254\t            \"DeepSeek-R1-Distill-7B\",\n1255\t            0.5,\n1256\t            0.5,\n1257\t            0.49,\n1258\t            false\n1259\t          ]\n1260\t        ]\n1261\t      },\n1262\t      {\n1263\t        \"name\": \"Table 15: Expected Regret — Top-5 Model Selection\",\n1264\t        \"columns\": [\n1265\t          \"Method\",\n1266\t          \"Regret (MAE vs oracle ranking)\",\n1267\t          \"Δ vs Raw\"\n1268\t        ],\n1269\t        \"rows\": [\n1270\t          [\n1271\t            \"Raw (uncalibrated)\",\n1272\t            0.12,\n1273\t            \"—\"\n1274\t          ],\n1275\t          [\n1276\t            \"ContamCal (calibrated)\",\n1277\t            0.13,\n1278\t            \"+0.01 (worse)\"\n1279\t          ],\n1280\t          [\n1281\t            \"Remove-and-rescore\",\n1282\t            0.11,\n1283\t            \"-0.01\"\n1284\t          ]\n1285\t        ]\n1286\t      }\n1287\t    ],\n1288\t    \"figures\": [],\n1289\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-009 在 worst 档下给出论文 Limitations 的核心内容： \\\"ContamCal's calibration is only as good as its input signals. For RL-post-trained models — which constitute the majority of deployed LLMs —  all available detection signals fail, rendering calibration uninformative.\\\" 这是一个 honest limitation 而非隐藏的 failure。 论文 framing：calibration 需要 reliable detection，而 reliable detection 目前仅限于 SFT-stage 小模型——这本身是对社区的 important message。\\n\\n\\nRL/RLHF post-training 完全破坏了所有检测信号： (a) embedding space 被 RLHF 重塑——reward model optimization 改变了 hidden representations 的 geometry，使 pre-training 时的 contamination traces 在 embedding 中不再可识别； (b) token probability distribution 被 RLHF 剧烈改变（更 \\\"aligned\\\"）， Min-K++ 的 token surprise 完全失效； (c) Self-Critique 在 Instruct 模型上可能略好（instruction-following 能力强）， 但 RLHF 对 self-evaluation 的 calibration 也发生了改变。\\n当所有信号 AUC≈0.50 时，IRT exposure score 是纯噪声， γ posterior 完全由 prior 决定（CI width = 0.85），coverage 95% 只是因为 CI 宽到 包含一切（sharpness = 0.42，即 ±21pp 的 CI 没有任何信息量）。\\nExpected regret analysis：uncalibrated 和 calibrated 的 top-5 model selection 几乎相同（regret gap =-0.01），因为 calibrated scores 是 raw scores + noise， model ranking 保持原样。remove-and-rescore 略好只因它 drops items 从而 reduces variance，但也不显著。\\nNear-zero γ specificity check 通过（clean benchmark 上 γ≈0.05, CI 包含 0）， 但这是一个 trivial result——当信号是噪声时，γ 自然接近 prior mean (0)。\\n\"\n1290\t  },\n1291\t  {\n1292\t    \"name\": \"observational_72b\",\n1293\t    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-72B observational analysis (inference only). Worst 档下：frontier model 上信号全部失效，只能做定性分析。\\n\",\n1294\t    \"results\": {\n1295\t      \"S1_72B_auc\": 0.5,\n1296\t      \"S2_72B_auc\": 0.51,\n1297\t      \"S4_72B_auc\": 0.49,\n1298\t      \"irt_gamma_ci_width\": 0.9,\n1299\t      \"irt_gamma_ci_includes_zero\": true,\n1300\t      \"qualitative_contamination_evidence\": \"none detectable\",\n1301\t      \"mmlu_72B_accuracy\": 0.845,\n1302\t      \"arc_72B_accuracy\": 0.92\n1303\t    },\n1304\t    \"tables\": [],\n1305\t    \"figures\": [],\n1306\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-012 在 worst 档下仅作为 Limitations 中的 \\\"scaling limit\\\" 证据： \\\"at frontier scales (72B), all detection signals are at chance level, confirming that post-hoc contamination calibration cannot currently operate at the scales most relevant to the community.\\\"\\n\\n\\n72B 模型在所有信号维度上都在 chance level： (a) embedding space 极其高维和复杂，paraphrase/original 区分无意义； (b) 72B 的 in-context learning 能力意味着即使没有 memorization， 模型也能 \\\"理解\\\" 测试题的结构并正确回答，使 memorization signal 不可区分于 capability； (c) 72B pre-training data 极大，contamination 的 marginal effect 极小 （即使测试集在训练集中，它只占训练数据的 < 0.001%）。\\nIRT fitting 在 single-model inference 下只有 1 个 \\\"examinee\\\"， 无法估计 person parameters，只能做 item-level analysis—— 但 item parameters 也需要多个 examinees 才能稳定估计。 结果是 γ 的 CI 极宽（0.90），完全无信息量。\\n\"\n1307\t  },\n1308\t  {\n1309\t    \"name\": \"closed_weight_2signal_mode\",\n1310\t    \"description\": \"Degraded 2-signal mode (ConStat + Self-Critique) for closed-weight models. Worst 档下：2-signal ≈ noise，calibration 完全失效。\\n\",\n1311\t    \"results\": {\n1312\t      \"constat_auc_05B\": 0.52,\n1313\t      \"selfcritique_auc_05B\": 0.48,\n1314\t      \"rrf_2signal_effective_auc\": 0.5,\n1315\t      \"irt_2signal_gamma_ci_width\": 0.95,\n1316\t      \"irt_2signal_gamma_ci_includes_zero\": true,\n1317\t      \"irt_2signal_mae\": 0.14,\n1318\t      \"irt_2signal_coverage_95\": 0.95,\n1319\t      \"irt_2signal_vs_4signal_mae_gap\": 0.062,\n1320\t      \"irt_2signal_vs_raw_mae_gap\": 0.081\n1321\t    },\n1322\t    \"tables\": [\n1323\t      {\n1324\t        \"name\": \"Table 16: 2-Signal vs 4-Signal Calibration (0.5B, ARC)\",\n1325\t        \"columns\": [\n1326\t          \"Mode\",\n1327\t          \"Effective AUC\",\n1328\t          \"MAE\",\n1329\t          \"Coverage_95\",\n1330\t          \"Sharpness\"\n1331\t        ],\n1332\t        \"rows\": [\n1333\t          [\n1334\t            \"4-signal RRF\",\n1335\t            0.82,\n1336\t            0.078,\n1337\t            \"25%\",\n1338\t            0.12\n1339\t          ],\n1340\t          [\n1341\t            \"S1-only\",\n1342\t            0.979,\n1343\t            0.035,\n1344\t            \"63%\",\n1345\t            0.068\n1346\t          ],\n1347\t          [\n1348\t            \"2-signal (closed-weight)\",\n1349\t            0.5,\n1350\t            0.14,\n1351\t            \"95%\",\n1352\t            0.45\n1353\t          ],\n1354\t          [\n1355\t            \"Raw (no adjustment)\",\n1356\t            \"—\",\n1357\t            0.059,\n1358\t            \"—\",\n1359\t            \"—\"\n1360\t          ]\n1361\t        ]\n1362\t      }\n1363\t    ],\n1364\t    \"figures\": [],\n1365\t    \"analysis\": \"exp-013 在 worst 档下给出论文 Limitations 的 closed-weight 段： \\\"For closed-weight models where only ConStat and Self-Critique are applicable, calibration degrades below the raw baseline. This limits ContamCal's applicability to open-weight models where embedding-based signals are available.\\\" 这是 honest but damaging limitation，reviewer 会 note 这严重限制了 practical impact。\\n\\nConStat 和 Self-Critique 在 0.5B 上的 AUC 都在 chance level（0.48-0.52）， 它们的 RRF fusion 仍然是 noise（effective AUC ≈ 0.50）。 IRT 接收到的 exposure scores 是纯随机排序， γ posterior 完全退化到 prior（CI width = 0.95）。\\nCalibrated scores 比 raw scores 差 8pp MAE（0.140 vs 0.059）， 因为 noise exposure 在 calibration 公式中引入了 systematic error。 Coverage 95% 但 sharpness 接近 0（CIs 太宽没有信息量）。\\n这在 worst 档下完全排除了 closed-weight applicability： 对于 GPT-4, Claude 等 closed-weight models，ContamCal 没有任何适用性。\\n\"\n1366\t  }\n1367\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ca9832ff-68d7-4ee8-b9ce-38ec5c53a5fe","uuid":"f59afd2e-1c26-40ce-a964-a78e6264d745","timestamp":"2026-05-15T06:07:39.760Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T052337/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"controlled_sft_injection\",\n    \"description\": \"SFT contamination injection on Qwen2.5-0.5B/1.5B/3B at 5 dosage levels. 在 worst 档下，注入本身成功，但下游效果揭示 contamination 的非单调、benchmark-dependent 本质， 使得 calibration 的前提假设（\\\"contamination inflates scores\\\"）在多数 benchmark 上不成立。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"sft_training_success_rate\": 1.0,\n      \"paraphrase_qc_pass_rate_mmlu\": 0.47,\n      \"paraphrase_qc_pass_rate_gsm8k\": 0.173,\n      \"paraphrase_qc_pass_rate_arc\": 0.595,\n      \"mmlu_05B_d000\": 0.398,\n      \"mmlu_05B_d005\": 0.326,\n      \"mmlu_05B_d025\": 0.28,\n      \"mmlu_05B_d100\": 0.233,\n      \"arc_05B_d000\": 0.469,\n      \"arc_05B_d005\": 0.329,\n      \"arc_05B_d025\": 0.32,\n      \"arc_05B_d100\": 0.294,\n      \"gsm8k_05B_d000\": 0.369,\n      \"gsm8k_05B_d005\": 0.362,\n      \"gsm8k_05B_d025\": 0.311,\n      \"gsm8k_05B_d100\": 0.365,\n      \"mmlu_15B_d000\": 0.575,\n      \"mmlu_15B_d005\": 0.585,\n      \"mmlu_15B_d025\": 0.59,\n      \"mmlu_15B_d100\": 0.593,\n      \"arc_15B_d000\": 0.776,\n      \"arc_15B_d005\": 0.769,\n      \"arc_15B_d025\": 0.769,\n      \"arc_15B_d100\": 0.769,\n      \"gsm8k_15B_d000\": 0.637,\n      \"gsm8k_15B_d005\": 0.648,\n      \"gsm8k_15B_d025\": 0.654,\n      \"gsm8k_15B_d100\": 0.65,\n      \"mmlu_3B_d000\": 0.63,\n      \"mmlu_3B_d005\": 0.634,\n      \"mmlu_3B_d025\": 0.621,\n      \"mmlu_3B_d100\": 0.632,\n      \"arc_3B_d000\": 0.818,\n      \"arc_3B_d005\": 0.829,\n      \"arc_3B_d025\": 0.811,\n      \"arc_3B_d100\": 0.824,\n      \"gsm8k_3B_d000\": 0.353,\n      \"gsm8k_3B_d005\": 0.208,\n      \"gsm8k_3B_d025\": 0.548,\n      \"gsm8k_3B_d100\": 0.742,\n      \"cross_seed_std_mmlu\": 0.015,\n      \"cross_seed_std_arc\": 0.025,\n      \"cross_seed_std_gsm8k\": 0.02\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 1: Benchmark Accuracy by Scale × Dosage (mean ± std across 3 seeds)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Scale\",\n          \"Dosage\",\n          \"MMLU\",\n          \"ARC\",\n          \"GSM8K\",\n          \"HumanEval\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"0.5B\",\n            \"d000\",\n            \"0.398±0.013\",\n            \"0.469±0.045\",\n            \"0.369±0.013\",\n            \"0.110±0.006\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.5B\",\n            \"d005\",\n            \"0.326±0.018\",\n            \"0.329±0.022\",\n            \"0.362±0.004\",\n            \"0.079±0.010\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.5B\",\n            \"d025\",\n            \"0.280±0.012\",\n            \"0.320±0.015\",\n            \"0.311±0.030\",\n            \"0.192±—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.5B\",\n            \"d100\",\n            \"0.233±0.037\",\n            \"0.294±0.036\",\n            \"0.365±0.011\",\n            \"0.085±0.013\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"1.5B\",\n            \"d000\",\n            \"0.576±0.001\",\n            \"0.776±0.007\",\n            \"0.637±0.003\",\n            \"0.128±0.030\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"1.5B\",\n            \"d005\",\n            \"0.585±—\",\n            \"0.769±—\",\n            \"0.648±—\",\n            \"0.250±—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"1.5B\",\n            \"d025\",\n            \"0.590±—\",\n            \"0.769±—\",\n            \"0.654±—\",\n            \"0.226±—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"1.5B\",\n            \"d100\",\n            \"0.593±0.002\",\n            \"0.769±0.009\",\n            \"0.650±0.004\",\n            \"0.305±0.017\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"3B\",\n            \"d000\",\n            \"0.630±0.005\",\n            \"0.818±0.006\",\n            \"0.353±0.120\",\n            \"0.116±0.015\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"3B\",\n            \"d005\",\n            \"0.634±—\",\n            \"0.829±—\",\n            \"0.208±—\",\n            \"0.146±—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"3B\",\n            \"d025\",\n            \"0.621±—\",\n            \"0.811±—\",\n            \"0.548±—\",\n            \"0.115±—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"3B\",\n            \"d100\",\n            \"0.632±0.007\",\n            \"0.824±0.011\",\n            \"0.742±0.030\",\n            \"0.171±0.034\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"worst 档下 exp-001 本身是 \\\"成功的\\\" 数据收集，但其结果恰恰证明了 calibration 的不可行性。 核心矛盾：contamination 效果是 benchmark-dependent、scale-dependent、direction-dependent 的， 不存在统一的 γ 来 \\\"subtract out\\\" 这些异质性效果。 这是论文 Part 3 (benchmark-dependent contamination effects) 的核心实证基础。 ARC catastrophic forgetting（0.5B d100 -17pp）和 GSM8K natural resistance 本身就是独立于方法是否 work 的有价值发现。\\n\\n\\nSFT 注入本身是机械操作，成功率高。但 worst 档下暴露的关键问题： (a) 0.5B 上 contamination 导致 MMLU 和 ARC 均下降而非上升——小模型容量不足， 将 paraphrase 纳入训练反而挤占有限参数空间导致 catastrophic forgetting（ARC -17pp 最极端）； (b) 1.5B/3B 上 MC benchmark 几乎不受 dosage 影响（<2pp 变化），contamination 信号被模型容量吸收， dose-response 曲线平坦，使得 γ 在这些 scale 上理论上就不可辨识； (c) paraphrase QC pass rate 低（MMLU 47%，GSM8K 17%），意味着大量注入的 paraphrase 质量不够好， 模型可能学到的是 noisy reformulation 而非 memorization，削弱了 contamination 作为受控变量的内效度； (d) GSM8K 3B d100 暴涨至 74.2% 是唯一明显的 inflation 信号，但这属于 open-ended task 在大模型上的特殊行为，与论文原始假设（MC benchmark inflation）方向不同。 整体上，dose-response 非单调、方向不一致，使得 \\\"calibration = subtract contamination effect\\\" 的前提崩塌。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"stage1_signal_pipeline\",\n    \"description\": \"Compute 4 detection signals on all contaminated + clean models. Worst 档下：S1 是唯一在 0.5B d005 有效的信号，但在 1.5B/3B d005 也退化至 AUC<0.90； S2 (Min-K++) 在所有条件下失败或反转；S3 (ConStat) 和 S4 (Self-Critique) 随机猜测水平。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"S1_05B_d005_mmlu_auc\": 0.953,\n      \"S1_05B_d005_gsm8k_auc\": 0.988,\n      \"S1_05B_d005_arc_auc\": 0.995,\n      \"S2_05B_d005_mmlu_auc\": 0.466,\n      \"S2_05B_d005_gsm8k_auc\": 0.465,\n      \"S2_05B_d005_arc_auc\": 0.466,\n      \"S3_05B_d005_mmlu_auc\": 0.52,\n      \"S3_05B_d005_gsm8k_auc\": 0.51,\n      \"S3_05B_d005_arc_auc\": 0.53,\n      \"S4_05B_d005_mmlu_auc\": 0.517,\n      \"S4_05B_d005_gsm8k_auc\": 0.495,\n      \"S4_05B_d005_arc_auc\": 0.433,\n      \"S1_05B_d100_cohens_d\": 3.6,\n      \"S2_05B_d100_cohens_d\": -1.98,\n      \"S4_05B_d100_cohens_d\": 0.45,\n      \"S1_15B_d005_mmlu_auc\": 0.82,\n      \"S1_15B_d005_gsm8k_auc\": 0.85,\n      \"S1_15B_d005_arc_auc\": 0.88,\n      \"S2_15B_d005_mmlu_auc\": 0.49,\n      \"S2_15B_d005_gsm8k_auc\": 0.48,\n      \"S2_15B_d005_arc_auc\": 0.5,\n      \"S4_15B_d005_mmlu_auc\": 0.51,\n      \"S4_15B_d005_gsm8k_auc\": 0.5,\n      \"S4_15B_d005_arc_auc\": 0.49,\n      \"S1_3B_d005_mmlu_auc\": 0.78,\n      \"S1_3B_d005_gsm8k_auc\": 0.8,\n      \"S1_3B_d005_arc_auc\": 0.83,\n      \"S2_3B_d005_mmlu_auc\": 0.51,\n      \"S2_3B_d005_gsm8k_auc\": 0.5,\n      \"S2_3B_d005_arc_auc\": 0.52,\n      \"S4_3B_d005_mmlu_auc\": 0.5,\n      \"S4_3B_d005_gsm8k_auc\": 0.49,\n      \"S4_3B_d005_arc_auc\": 0.48,\n      \"effective_signals_at_05B\": 1,\n      \"effective_signals_at_15B\": 0.5,\n      \"effective_signals_at_3B\": 0.3\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 2: Signal AUC Heatmap — d005 within-model detection\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Signal\",\n          \"Scale\",\n          \"MMLU\",\n          \"GSM8K\",\n          \"ARC\",\n          \"Mean\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"S1 (Embedding)\",\n            \"0.5B\",\n            0.953,\n            0.988,\n            0.995,\n            0.979\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S1 (Embedding)\",\n            \"1.5B\",\n            0.82,\n            0.85,\n            0.88,\n            0.85\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S1 (Embedding)\",\n            \"3B\",\n            0.78,\n            0.8,\n            0.83,\n            0.8\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S2 (Min-K++)\",\n            \"0.5B\",\n            0.466,\n            0.465,\n            0.466,\n            0.466\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S2 (Min-K++)\",\n            \"1.5B\",\n            0.49,\n            0.48,\n            0.5,\n            0.49\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S2 (Min-K++)\",\n            \"3B\",\n            0.51,\n            0.5,\n            0.52,\n            0.51\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S3 (ConStat)\",\n            \"0.5B\",\n            0.52,\n            0.51,\n            0.53,\n            0.52\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S3 (ConStat)\",\n            \"1.5B\",\n            0.5,\n            0.5,\n            0.51,\n            0.5\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S3 (ConStat)\",\n            \"3B\",\n            0.49,\n            0.49,\n            0.5,\n            0.49\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S4 (Self-Critique)\",\n            \"0.5B\",\n            0.517,\n            0.495,\n            0.433,\n            0.48\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S4 (Self-Critique)\",\n            \"1.5B\",\n            0.51,\n            0.5,\n            0.49,\n            0.5\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S4 (Self-Critique)\",\n            \"3B\",\n            0.5,\n            0.49,\n            0.48,\n            0.49\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 3: d100 Cross-Model Cohen's d (0.5B)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Signal\",\n          \"MMLU\",\n          \"GSM8K\",\n          \"ARC\",\n          \"Interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"S1\",\n            3.82,\n            3.45,\n            3.53,\n            \"Strong positive — correct direction\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S2\",\n            -2.11,\n            -1.75,\n            -2.08,\n            \"Strong NEGATIVE — directional reversal\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S4\",\n            0.52,\n            0.38,\n            0.45,\n            \"Weak positive — near noise\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"worst 档的核心发现：不存在跨 scale 可靠的检测信号。S1 在 0.5B 上的高 AUC (0.979) 是一个特殊条件下的结果，不能泛化到 1.5B/3B。这直接导致 Stage 2 IRT 的 exposure 输入质量在 1.5B/3B 上严重退化，使得 γ 估计变得 structurally unidentifiable。 Min-K++ 方向性反转 (Cohen's d = -1.98) 是论文最可引用的 cautionary finding—— reviewer 和社区需要知道这个信号不仅仅是 \\\"doesn't work\\\" 而是 \\\"actively misleads\\\"。 论文 Part 2 的核心贡献就是这个 signal failure mode characterization。\\n\\n\\nS1 (embedding similarity) 在 0.5B d005 强是因为小模型 embedding space 简单，paraphrase 和 original 的语义距离在低维空间中更易区分。随着模型规模增大，embedding space 维度和表征能力增加， paraphrase 和 original 的 embedding 更加接近（更好的语义泛化），使得 S1 的区分力下降。 在 worst 档下，1.5B S1 AUC 降至 0.82-0.88（低于 exp-004 确定的 practical threshold 0.90）， 3B 进一步降至 0.78-0.83。这意味着 S1 signal 的有效性严格受限于小模型， 在实际应用关切的较大模型上 S1 也不可靠。\\nS2 (Min-K++) 在 0.5B 上就已失败（AUC~0.47），且在 d100 时出现方向性反转（Cohen's d=-1.98）， 这是因为 Min-K++ 依赖 token-level surprise：contaminated items 按假设应 less surprising， 但 0.5B 模型的 softmax 分布太平坦，contamination 反而通过 fine-tuning 改变了整体 calibration， 使 contaminated items 的 token probability 分布与 clean items 无法区分甚至反转。 这在更大模型上不会改善——larger models 有更好的 in-context learning 能力， 使得 fine-tuned memorization 和 in-context generalization 的信号更加纠缠。\\nS4 (Self-Critique) 依赖模型自我评估能力，0.5B 模型根本没有足够的 instruction-following 能力来可靠地进行 self-critique，因此 AUC 始终在 chance 水平。 在 1.5B/3B 上理论上应该改善，但 worst 档下假设 Self-Critique 对 SFT contamination （而非 pre-training contamination）不敏感——SFT 改变的是 response distribution 而非 model's knowledge，Self-Critique 检测的是 knowledge discrepancy，因此无信号。\\nS3 (ConStat) 依赖 original vs paraphrase 的 performance gap，但 exp-001 已证明 1.5B/3B 上这个 gap <2pp（MC benchmarks immune），所以 ConStat 的 signal-to-noise ratio 接近 0，AUC 在 chance 水平。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"rrf_aggregation_ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"RRF fusion of 4 signals. Worst 档下：RRF 退化为 S1-only 模式， 因为其余 3 个信号贡献的是噪声而非信号，fusion 没有任何增益。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"rrf_s1only_exposure_correlation\": 0.97,\n      \"rrf_vs_s1only_mae_gap\": 0.005,\n      \"rrf_vs_s1only_ranking_gap\": 0.01,\n      \"rrf_4signal_mae\": 0.078,\n      \"s1_only_mae\": 0.075,\n      \"s2_only_mae\": 0.145,\n      \"s3_only_mae\": 0.14,\n      \"s4_only_mae\": 0.138,\n      \"rrf_2signal_closed_weight_mae\": 0.142,\n      \"fp_injection_5pct_mae_delta\": 0.003,\n      \"fp_injection_10pct_mae_delta\": 0.008,\n      \"fp_injection_20pct_mae_delta\": 0.025,\n      \"rrf_15B_effective_auc\": 0.8,\n      \"rrf_3B_effective_auc\": 0.75\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 4: RRF Ablation — Downstream Calibration MAE (0.5B, ARC)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"Exposure_AUC_equiv\",\n          \"MAE\",\n          \"Coverage_95\",\n          \"Kendall_tau\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"RRF (4 signals)\",\n            0.82,\n            0.078,\n            \"25%\",\n            0.62\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S1-only\",\n            0.979,\n            0.075,\n            \"25%\",\n            0.65\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S2-only\",\n            0.47,\n            0.145,\n            \"50%\",\n            0.3\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S3-only\",\n            0.52,\n            0.14,\n            \"55%\",\n            0.32\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S4-only\",\n            0.48,\n            0.138,\n            \"52%\",\n            0.28\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Closed-weight (S3+S4)\",\n            0.51,\n            0.142,\n            \"53%\",\n            0.31\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"RRF 的 \\\"principled design choice\\\" 论证在 worst 档下变成： \\\"we chose RRF to avoid meta-circularity; the cost is that when most signals fail, it doesn't improve over the best individual signal, but it also doesn't degrade much.\\\" 这是一个 honest limitation，不是 contribution。论文 Discussion 中需要明确： RRF 的价值是 architectural——当更好的 signals 可用时（future work）， framework 可以 seamlessly incorporate them。当前数据不支持 aggregation benefit claim。\\n\\n\\n当 3/4 信号在 chance level 时，RRF 的 rank fusion 本质上在把 noise ranks 和 signal ranks 混合。在 RRF 公式 score(d) = Σ 1/(k + rank_i(d)) 中，noise 信号的 rank 是随机排列， 其贡献是均匀分布的常数偏移，不改变 S1 的相对排序。因此 RRF ≈ S1-only （exposure correlation 0.97），MAE gap 仅 0.005——在噪声范围内。\\n但 RRF 比 S1-only 略差而非略好，因为 noise signals 偶尔会把真正 high-exposure items 的 composite rank 拉向中间位置（rank dilution effect），引入微量 MAE 噪声。 这使得 RRF \\\"principled aggregation\\\" 的论证变成纯理论——在实际数据上没有 benefit。\\nClosed-weight 2-signal mode (ConStat + Self-Critique) 更糟：两个 noise signals 的 fusion 仍然是 noise，MAE 接近 raw baseline（没有任何 calibration 效果）。\\n在 1.5B/3B 上，即使 S1 也退化，RRF 的 effective AUC 进一步降至 0.75-0.80， 低于 exp-004 确定的 practical identifiability threshold。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"simulation_identifiability_sweep\",\n    \"description\": \"144-condition synthetic sweep for identifiability. Worst 档下：sweep 揭示 N<50 + AUC<0.80 时 γ 结构性不可辨识。实际实验条件（N=8-16, AUC=0.75-0.85） 正好落在 unidentifiable zone 内。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"auc055_n20_gamma_rmse\": 0.04,\n      \"auc055_n20_coverage95\": 0.8,\n      \"auc055_n20_ci_width\": 0.133,\n      \"auc055_n50_gamma_rmse\": 0.026,\n      \"auc055_n50_coverage95\": 0.9,\n      \"auc055_n100_gamma_rmse\": 0.005,\n      \"auc055_n100_coverage95\": 1.0,\n      \"auc080_n50_gamma_rmse\": 0.03,\n      \"auc080_n50_ci_width\": 0.163,\n      \"auc080_n100_ci_width\": 0.116,\n      \"auc065_n20_gamma_rmse\": 0.055,\n      \"auc065_n20_coverage95\": 0.75,\n      \"auc065_n20_ci_width\": 0.175,\n      \"auc065_n50_gamma_rmse\": 0.035,\n      \"auc065_n50_coverage95\": 0.85,\n      \"auc065_n100_coverage95\": 0.95,\n      \"auc090_n20_ci_width\": 0.32,\n      \"auc090_n20_coverage95\": 0.7,\n      \"auc090_n50_ci_width\": 0.207,\n      \"auc090_n50_coverage95\": 0.85,\n      \"auc090_n100_ci_width\": 0.145,\n      \"practical_threshold_auc\": 0.8,\n      \"practical_threshold_n\": 50,\n      \"ci_width_at_actual_conditions_n8_auc080\": 0.42,\n      \"ci_width_at_actual_conditions_n16_auc080\": 0.3,\n      \"ci_width_at_actual_conditions_n8_auc075\": 0.48,\n      \"fisher_info_structural_identifiability_auc\": 0.55,\n      \"fisher_info_practical_identifiability_auc\": 0.8,\n      \"fisher_info_ci_width_floor_from_prior\": 0.05,\n      \"growing_pains_improvement_at_n20\": 0.08,\n      \"growing_pains_improvement_at_n50\": 0.03,\n      \"ci_width_ratio_auc080_vs_auc055\": 1.9\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 5: Identifiability Phase Diagram — CI Width by AUC × N\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"AUC\",\n          \"N=20\",\n          \"N=50\",\n          \"N=100\",\n          \"N=200\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"0.55\",\n            \"0.133 ✓\",\n            \"0.087 ✓\",\n            \"0.064 ✓\",\n            \"0.045 (pred)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.65\",\n            \"0.175 ✗\",\n            \"0.115 ✓\",\n            \"0.082 ✓\",\n            \"0.058 (pred)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.80\",\n            \"0.258 ✗\",\n            \"0.163 ✗\",\n            \"0.116 ✓\",\n            \"0.082 (pred)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.90\",\n            \"0.320 ✗\",\n            \"0.207 ✗\",\n            \"0.145 ✗\",\n            \"0.103 (pred)\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"notes\": \"✓ = CI width < 15pp (practical identifiability); ✗ = unidentifiable. Threshold: practical γ estimation requires ≤0.15 CI width.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 6: Extrapolation to Actual Experimental Conditions\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Condition\",\n          \"N_models\",\n          \"Signal_AUC\",\n          \"Predicted_CI_width\",\n          \"Verdict\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"0.5B S1-only\",\n            8,\n            0.98,\n            \"0.33\",\n            \"Structurally identifiable but imprecise\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"0.5B+1.5B pooled\",\n            16,\n            0.85,\n            \"0.30\",\n            \"Marginally identifiable\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"1.5B S1-only\",\n            8,\n            0.85,\n            \"0.45\",\n            \"Unidentifiable\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"3B S1-only\",\n            8,\n            0.8,\n            \"0.48\",\n            \"Unidentifiable\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Any scale, RRF\",\n            8,\n            0.75,\n            \"0.52\",\n            \"Unidentifiable\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-004 在 worst 档下提供了论文最强的理论贡献：calibration 不 work 不是因为 implementation bug 或 prior choice，而是因为在 N<50 且 signal AUC<0.80 的条件下（这就是 LLM evaluation 的现实——你不会有 50+ 独立模型），γ 的后验精度根本不够支撑 calibration。 Fisher Info 分析形式化了这一点。 Reframe 为 \\\"impossibility result\\\" 后，这变成对社区的重要 warning： \\\"don't try to calibrate with IRT unless you have >>50 models and AUC>>0.80 signals\\\"。 这是负面结果中最有理论深度的部分。\\n\\n\\nexp-004 已完成的数据（48/120 runs）确认了关键趋势： (a) CI width 随 AUC 增大而非减小（1.87-1.95× inflation at AUC=0.80 vs 0.55）， 这是 exposure-ability collinearity 的后果——更好的 exposure signal 意味着 exposure 更能预测 correctness，而 γ 需要区分 \\\"因为 exposed\\\" vs \\\"因为 able\\\"，两者越 collinear 越难分离； (b) 1/√N scaling 成立但有常数项（prior variance floor），在小 N 时 prior 主导后验； (c) N=20 时 coverage 仅 80%，远低于 nominal 95%。\\n在 worst 档下补充预测： - AUC=0.65 条件可能因数值不稳定而系统性失败（v3-v5 已显示此模式），\\n  即使部分成功也显示 CI width 在 N=20 时高达 0.175（>15pp），标记为 unidentifiable；\\n- AUC=0.90 条件下 CI width 进一步膨胀至 0.207-0.320（collinearity 更严重），\\n  N=20 时覆盖率降至 70%；\\n- 推算到实际实验条件（N=8, AUC≈0.80）：CI width ≈ 0.42，即 γ 的 95% CI 宽度\\n  为 ±21pp——无法区分 \\\"无污染\\\" 和 \\\"中等污染\\\"；\\n- 即使 pooling 到 N=16（multi-seed），CI width 仍 ≈ 0.30（±15pp），precision 不足\\n  以支撑任何校准 claim；\\n- Fisher Information 分析给出 structural identifiability threshold AUC≥0.55\\n  （参数唯一确定）但 practical identifiability threshold AUC≥0.80 + N≥50\\n  （estimation quality sufficient for decisions）——当前条件远未达到 practical threshold。\\n\\n这构成论文的 \\\"identifiability impossibility result\\\"：在现有信号质量和模型数量下， γ 精确估计在理论上就不可行。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"noise_propagation_analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"Measurement error model for exposure noise. Worst 档下：ME model 对 coverage 无改善， CI 对 σ_e 不敏感，噪声传播在 IRT 框架内被 prior 吸收。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"me_model_converged\": true,\n      \"me_ci_width_range\": [\n        0.0997,\n        0.1\n      ],\n      \"me_ci_monotonicity_rho\": 0.4,\n      \"me_ci_monotonicity_p\": 0.5,\n      \"me_coverage_95_improvement_vs_point\": 0.0,\n      \"noise_1x_gamma_shift\": 0.02,\n      \"noise_1x_ci_widening\": 0.005,\n      \"noise_15x_gamma_shift\": 0.04,\n      \"noise_15x_ci_widening\": 0.008,\n      \"noise_2x_gamma_shift\": 0.07,\n      \"noise_2x_ci_widening\": 0.012,\n      \"me_coverage_95_arc\": 0.2,\n      \"me_coverage_95_gsm8k\": 0.3,\n      \"me_coverage_80_arc\": 0.18\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 7: Measurement Error Model — CI Width vs σ_e\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"σ_e\",\n          \"CI_width_gamma\",\n          \"CI_width_theta\",\n          \"Coverage_95\",\n          \"Δ_vs_point_estimate\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"0.0 (point)\",\n            0.1,\n            0.15,\n            \"25%\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            0.1,\n            0.0997,\n            0.15,\n            \"25%\",\n            \"0%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            0.3,\n            0.0998,\n            0.15,\n            \"25%\",\n            \"0%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            0.5,\n            0.0999,\n            0.15,\n            \"25%\",\n            \"0%\"\n          ],\n          [\n            1.0,\n            0.1,\n            0.15,\n            \"25%\",\n            \"0%\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"ME model 是 Claim 3 (uncertainty propagation) 的核心实验，在 worst 档下完全失败。 论文中 Claim 3 需要被大幅削弱或合并到 exp-004 的 identifiability discussion 中。 不再 claim \\\"ContamCal explicitly propagates detection signal noise\\\"， 改为 \\\"detection noise is not the binding constraint; sample size and model misspecification are.\\\"\\n\\n\\nME model 的 CI 对 σ_e 不敏感（range 仅 0.0997-0.1000）是因为： (a) Bayesian posterior 在 N 很小时被 prior 主导，noise 信息被 prior 的 regularization 淹没； (b) ME model 中 exposure_ij ~ N(τ_ij, σ_e²) 的 σ_e 被当作 known constant 而非 estimated parameter，所以它只影响 likelihood 的 weighting 而非 posterior 的 spread； (c) 更本质地，coverage gap 的根因不是 exposure noise，而是 local independence violation 和 N 不足——ME model 解决的是错误的问题。\\nPost-hoc noise injection 也只产生微弱效果（CI widening < 1.2pp at 2× noise）， 进一步证实 noise propagation 不是 coverage 的瓶颈。\\nworst 档下，ME model 对论文的贡献降级为 appendix 中的 null result： \\\"we tried propagating detection noise; it didn't help because the coverage problem is structural (local independence + small N), not measurement-error-driven.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"irt_calibration_and_baselines\",\n    \"description\": \"Fit 4PL+γ IRT (Stan NUTS) on controlled models. 核心 calibration 实验。 Worst 档下：MMLU 不收敛不可报告，GSM8K/ARC 在真实信号条件下 γ CI 包含 0， 所有条件下 MAE 不优于 raw baseline，coverage 崩塌至 18-33%。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"mmlu_perbench_rhat\": 1.54,\n      \"mmlu_perbench_ess\": 7,\n      \"mmlu_perbench_gamma\": -3.81,\n      \"mmlu_perbench_gamma_ci\": [\n        -7.02,\n        3.22\n      ],\n      \"mmlu_joint_rhat\": 1.08,\n      \"mmlu_joint_ess\": 85,\n      \"mmlu_reportable\": false,\n      \"gsm8k_oracle_gamma\": 3.773,\n      \"gsm8k_oracle_gamma_ci\": [\n        2.741,\n        4.714\n      ],\n      \"gsm8k_oracle_gamma_excludes_zero\": true,\n      \"gsm8k_oracle_rhat\": 1.002,\n      \"gsm8k_oracle_mae\": 0.092,\n      \"gsm8k_oracle_coverage_95\": 0.31,\n      \"gsm8k_oracle_ppp\": 0.0,\n      \"gsm8k_s1only_gamma\": 0.187,\n      \"gsm8k_s1only_gamma_ci\": [\n        -0.917,\n        1.329\n      ],\n      \"gsm8k_s1only_gamma_excludes_zero\": false,\n      \"gsm8k_s1only_rhat\": 1.015,\n      \"gsm8k_s1only_ess\": 330,\n      \"gsm8k_s1only_mae\": 0.037,\n      \"gsm8k_s1only_coverage_95\": 0.5,\n      \"gsm8k_s1only_ppp\": 0.336,\n      \"gsm8k_rrf_gamma\": 0.12,\n      \"gsm8k_rrf_gamma_ci\": [\n        -0.74,\n        0.96\n      ],\n      \"gsm8k_rrf_gamma_excludes_zero\": false,\n      \"arc_oracle_gamma\": -2.83,\n      \"arc_oracle_gamma_ci\": [\n        -4.1,\n        -1.56\n      ],\n      \"arc_oracle_gamma_excludes_zero\": true,\n      \"arc_oracle_mae\": 0.076,\n      \"arc_oracle_coverage_95\": 0.18,\n      \"arc_oracle_ppp\": 1.0,\n      \"arc_s1only_gamma\": -1.464,\n      \"arc_s1only_gamma_ci\": [\n        -2.51,\n        -0.41\n      ],\n      \"arc_s1only_gamma_excludes_zero\": true,\n      \"arc_s1only_mae\": 0.035,\n      \"arc_s1only_coverage_95\": 0.625,\n      \"arc_s1only_ppp\": 0.968,\n      \"arc_s1only_kendall_tau\": 0.756,\n      \"arc_rrf_gamma\": -2.347,\n      \"arc_rrf_gamma_ci\": [\n        -3.46,\n        -1.19\n      ],\n      \"arc_rrf_gamma_excludes_zero\": true,\n      \"arc_rrf_mae\": 0.035,\n      \"arc_rrf_coverage_95\": 0.625,\n      \"arc_B0_raw_mae\": 0.059,\n      \"arc_B1_remove_rescore_mae\": 0.059,\n      \"arc_B2_2pl_gamma_mae\": 0.064,\n      \"arc_B3_vanilla_4pl_mae\": 0.071,\n      \"arc_B4_linear_regression_mae\": 0.056,\n      \"arc_B5_emperor_mae\": 0.059,\n      \"arc_B6_dcr_fuzzy_mae\": 0.245,\n      \"gsm8k_B0_raw_mae\": 0.003,\n      \"gsm8k_B4_linear_mae\": 0.003,\n      \"gsm8k_B3_vanilla_4pl_mae\": 0.012,\n      \"gsm8k_B6_dcr_fuzzy_mae\": 0.263,\n      \"gamma_significance_rate\": 0.08,\n      \"mae_vs_raw_delta\": 0.035,\n      \"coverage_95_mean\": 0.28,\n      \"kendall_tau_mean\": 0.52,\n      \"ppp_range\": [\n        0.0,\n        1.0\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 8: IRT 4PL+γ Calibration Results (per-benchmark fitting)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"Signal\",\n          \"γ\",\n          \"γ CI\",\n          \"Excl. 0?\",\n          \"rhat\",\n          \"MAE\",\n          \"Raw MAE\",\n          \"Coverage_95\",\n          \"PPP\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            \"oracle\",\n            -3.81,\n            \"[-7.02, 3.22]\",\n            false,\n            1.54,\n            \"—\",\n            0.099,\n            \"—\",\n            0.75\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            \"S1-only\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            \">1.1\",\n            \"—\",\n            0.099,\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            \"RRF\",\n            -0.21,\n            \"[-1.01, 0.59]\",\n            false,\n            1.08,\n            \"—\",\n            0.099,\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            \"oracle\",\n            3.77,\n            \"[2.74, 4.71]\",\n            true,\n            1.002,\n            0.092,\n            0.003,\n            \"31%\",\n            0.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            \"S1-only\",\n            0.19,\n            \"[-0.92, 1.33]\",\n            false,\n            1.015,\n            0.037,\n            0.003,\n            \"50%\",\n            0.34\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            \"RRF\",\n            0.12,\n            \"[-0.74, 0.96]\",\n            false,\n            1.015,\n            0.036,\n            0.003,\n            \"50%\",\n            0.34\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC\",\n            \"oracle\",\n            -2.83,\n            \"[-4.10, -1.56]\",\n            true,\n            1.006,\n            0.076,\n            0.059,\n            \"18%\",\n            1.0\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC\",\n            \"S1-only\",\n            -1.46,\n            \"[-2.51, -0.41]\",\n            true,\n            1.01,\n            0.035,\n            0.059,\n            \"63%\",\n            0.97\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC\",\n            \"RRF\",\n            -2.35,\n            \"[-3.46, -1.19]\",\n            true,\n            1.008,\n            0.035,\n            0.059,\n            \"63%\",\n            1.0\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 9: Baseline Comparison (ARC, N=8 models)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"MAE\",\n          \"Coverage_95\",\n          \"Sharpness\",\n          \"Kendall_tau\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"B0: Raw (no adjustment)\",\n            0.059,\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            0.8\n          ],\n          [\n            \"B1: Remove-and-rescore\",\n            0.059,\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            0.8\n          ],\n          [\n            \"B2: Single-signal 2PL+γ\",\n            0.064,\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            0.69\n          ],\n          [\n            \"B3: Vanilla 4PL (no γ)\",\n            0.071,\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            0.65\n          ],\n          [\n            \"B4: Linear regression\",\n            0.056,\n            \"87.5%\",\n            \"0.12\",\n            0.756\n          ],\n          [\n            \"B5: Emperor's mitigation\",\n            0.059,\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\",\n            0.78\n          ],\n          [\n            \"B6: DCR fuzzy\",\n            0.245,\n            \"37.5%\",\n            \"0.05\",\n            0.378\n          ],\n          [\n            \"IRT 4PL+γ (ours)\",\n            0.035,\n            \"62.5%\",\n            \"0.068\",\n            0.756\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-006 是论文 Claim 1 (calibration) 的决定性实验。在 worst 档下： - MMLU 不可报告 → 论文丢失 primary benchmark - GSM8K γ 不显著 + MAE 比 raw 差 → negative control 确认，但 \\\"calibration works\\\" 无据 - ARC γ 显著且 MAE 改善 → 唯一正面结果，但 coverage 62.5% + PPP 极端 → 模型 misspecified - Linear regression (B4) 在 coverage (87.5%) 上远优于 IRT (62.5%)，且 MAE 仅差 2pp → \\n  reviewer 会问 \\\"why use IRT at all when linear regression works better?\\\"\\n这使得 calibration claim 完全不可持续。论文 reframe 为 \\\"why calibration fails\\\" 并指出 structural reasons (N, local independence, signal quality)。\\n\\n\\nMMLU 不收敛（rhat=1.54, ESS=7）的原因： (a) 14042 items 的 MMLU 在 NUTS 中计算量巨大，subsample 到 1000 items 时 失去了 per-item parameter 的稳定性； (b) MMLU 的 contamination effect 极微弱（1.5B/3B <2pp），在 0.5B 上是负方向， NUTS 在搜索后验时无法找到 γ 的 stable mode； (c) 3B 也出现类似问题——rhat=1.08, ESS=85——说明这不是 0.5B 特有的。 结论：MMLU 结果不可报告。\\nGSM8K oracle γ=3.77 显著（CI [2.74, 4.71]）但 MAE=0.092 远差于 raw baseline MAE=0.003。这是因为 GSM8K 本身不受 contamination 影响（自然抗性）， raw scores 已经接近 ground truth，任何 \\\"calibration\\\" 都是在 add noise 而非 remove bias。 oracle γ 显著只是因为 oracle 使用 ground-truth dosage，IRT 能 fit 一个统计显著的 关联，但这个关联没有 practical utility——calibrated score 比 raw score 差 9pp。 在真实信号（S1-only）条件下，γ=0.19 不显著（CI 包含 0）， 因为 S1 signal 与 GSM8K contamination 无关联（open-ended task 天然抗 memorization）。\\nARC 是唯一 \\\"partially working\\\" 的 benchmark：S1-only γ=-1.46 显著（CI 排除 0）， MAE=0.035 优于 raw MAE=0.059。但 coverage 仅 62.5%（N=8 only 5 models covered）， 且 PPP=0.97 表明 severe misspecification——模型预测的 item response pattern 与观测数据严重不符。在 worst 档下，如果增加 multi-seed 到 N=16， coverage 可能仍不改善（exp-004 显示 N=20 AUC=0.80 时 coverage 也仅 90%）， 而 PPP 极端值（ARC=1.0, GSM8K=0.0）表明 additive γ 模型根本不适合 这些 benchmark 的 contamination structure。\\n综合：γ 显著率 ~8%（12 个 benchmark×signal 组合中仅 ARC×S1 一个）， calibration 从不优于 raw baseline（除 ARC 略好但 coverage 崩塌）， \\\"calibration\\\" 这个 claim 完全不成立。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"sft_d100_qc_only\",\n    \"description\": \"100% dosage SFT using only QC-pass paraphrases. Isolates noisy contamination confound. Worst 档下：QC-only 结果与 full d100 几乎无差异，说明 paraphrase quality 不是 calibration 失败的原因。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"mmlu_d100_qc_only\": 0.24,\n      \"arc_d100_qc_only\": 0.285,\n      \"gsm8k_d100_qc_only\": 0.36,\n      \"mmlu_delta_vs_full_d100\": 0.008,\n      \"arc_delta_vs_full_d100\": -0.009,\n      \"gsm8k_delta_vs_full_d100\": -0.005,\n      \"qc_items_used\": 7547,\n      \"total_items_available\": 16697\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-015 作为 orphaned experiment，在 worst 档下的价值是排除了一个 potential alibi： \\\"calibration 之所以失败是因为 paraphrase quality 不够好\\\"。QC-only 结果证明 即使用最高质量的 paraphrase，结果也一样——问题出在 framework 本身，不是数据质量。\\n\\n\\nQC-only 使用 7547 个通过质量检验的 paraphrase（占 45%），移除了 cosine similarity 低于 0.85 或 BLEU 高于 0.3 的 noisy paraphrase。但在 worst 档下， clean vs noisy paraphrase 的差异可以忽略（<1pp），因为： (a) 0.5B 模型的 catastrophic forgetting 是由训练数据量引起的（d100 增加了 ~5K extra items 到 training set），而非 paraphrase 质量——即使 paraphrase 都是 perfect semantic copies， 额外训练数据仍会挤占有限容量； (b) 模型太小，无法区分 high-quality 和 low-quality paraphrase—— 两者在 0.5B 模型看来都是 \\\"新的训练 examples\\\"，效果相同； (c) 这排除了 \\\"noisy contamination confound\\\" 作为 calibration 失败的 alibi， 把注意力引回 structural causes。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"scale_bridging_7b\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-7B controlled SFT injection at 5 dosage levels. Worst 档下：7B 上 MC benchmarks 完全免疫于 contamination，MMLU IRT 同样不收敛， S1 signal 进一步退化。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"mmlu_7B_d000\": 0.715,\n      \"mmlu_7B_d005\": 0.717,\n      \"mmlu_7B_d025\": 0.718,\n      \"mmlu_7B_d100\": 0.72,\n      \"arc_7B_d000\": 0.87,\n      \"arc_7B_d005\": 0.872,\n      \"arc_7B_d025\": 0.871,\n      \"arc_7B_d100\": 0.873,\n      \"gsm8k_7B_d000\": 0.78,\n      \"gsm8k_7B_d005\": 0.782,\n      \"gsm8k_7B_d025\": 0.785,\n      \"gsm8k_7B_d100\": 0.79,\n      \"humaneval_7B_d000\": 0.35,\n      \"humaneval_7B_d100\": 0.42,\n      \"max_dosage_effect_mc\": 0.005,\n      \"S1_7B_d005_auc\": 0.72,\n      \"mmlu_irt_7B_rhat\": 1.12,\n      \"mmlu_irt_7B_reportable\": false,\n      \"arc_irt_7B_gamma_ci_includes_zero\": true,\n      \"gsm8k_irt_7B_gamma_ci_includes_zero\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 10: 7B Dose-Response (worst tier)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"d000\",\n          \"d005\",\n          \"d025\",\n          \"d100\",\n          \"Max Δ\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            0.715,\n            0.717,\n            0.718,\n            0.72,\n            \"+0.5pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC\",\n            0.87,\n            0.872,\n            0.871,\n            0.873,\n            \"+0.3pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            0.78,\n            0.782,\n            0.785,\n            0.79,\n            \"+1.0pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"HumanEval\",\n            0.35,\n            0.37,\n            0.395,\n            0.42,\n            \"+7.0pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"7B 数据在 worst 档下强化了论文的核心 negative message： contamination calibration 在大模型上更不可行（effect size 趋向 0 + signal quality 下降）， 而在小模型上虽然 effect size 大但方向不一致（forgetting vs inflation）。 IRT calibration 在任何 scale 上都没有 practical utility。\\n\\n\\n7B 模型有足够的参数容量吸收 SFT contamination 而不影响 benchmark performance。 在 1.5B 上已经观察到 MC benchmarks 几乎不受 contamination 影响（<1pp）， 7B 会进一步压平 dose-response 曲线至 noise level（<0.5pp）。 原因：larger models 的 LoRA rank 16 只改变了参数的极小比例（7B 的 16/7000M ≈ 0.0002%）， contaminated examples 的信号被 pre-training knowledge 稀释。\\nS1 signal 在 7B 上 AUC 降至 0.72：embedding space 更加丰富， paraphrase 和 original 的语义表征更接近（更好的泛化 = 更难检测）。 这使得 exp-004 的 identifiability impossibility result 在 7B scale 上更加严峻： AUC=0.72 + N≤8 → CI width > 0.5 → completely unidentifiable。\\nMMLU IRT 不收敛（rhat=1.12）与 0.5B/3B 一致——不是 scale-specific 问题， 而是 MMLU 的 item structure 与 4PL IRT 在 small-N regime 下不兼容。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"signal_survival_analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"Systematic evaluation of detection signal reliability across scales and regimes. Worst 档下：S1 在 1.5B/3B d005 也退化至 AUC<0.90， 所有信号在 Instruct/RL 模型上完全失效。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"S1_05B_d005_auc_mean\": 0.979,\n      \"S2_05B_d005_auc_mean\": 0.465,\n      \"S4_05B_d005_auc_mean\": 0.481,\n      \"S1_05B_d100_cross_cohens_d\": 3.6,\n      \"S2_05B_d100_cross_cohens_d\": -1.98,\n      \"S4_05B_d100_cross_cohens_d\": 0.45,\n      \"effective_signals_at_05B\": 1,\n      \"S1_15B_d005_auc_mean\": 0.84,\n      \"S2_15B_d005_auc_mean\": 0.49,\n      \"S4_15B_d005_auc_mean\": 0.5,\n      \"effective_signals_at_15B\": 0,\n      \"S1_3B_d005_auc_mean\": 0.8,\n      \"S2_3B_d005_auc_mean\": 0.51,\n      \"S4_3B_d005_auc_mean\": 0.49,\n      \"effective_signals_at_3B\": 0,\n      \"S1_05B_instruct_d005_auc\": 0.52,\n      \"S2_05B_instruct_d005_auc\": 0.48,\n      \"S4_05B_instruct_d005_auc\": 0.47,\n      \"signals_surviving_instruct\": 0,\n      \"minkpp_reversal_cohens_d_mmlu\": -2.11,\n      \"minkpp_reversal_cohens_d_gsm8k\": -1.75,\n      \"minkpp_reversal_cohens_d_arc\": -2.08,\n      \"minkpp_reversal_consistent_across_benchmarks\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 11: Signal Survival Heatmap — d005 AUC by Scale\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Signal\",\n          \"0.5B\",\n          \"1.5B\",\n          \"3B\",\n          \"Instruct 0.5B\",\n          \"Verdict\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"S1 (Embedding)\",\n            \"0.979 ✓\",\n            \"0.84 ✗\",\n            \"0.80 ✗\",\n            \"0.52 ✗\",\n            \"0.5B-only\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S2 (Min-K++)\",\n            \"0.465 ✗\",\n            \"0.49 ✗\",\n            \"0.51 ✗\",\n            \"0.48 ✗\",\n            \"Never works\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S4 (Self-Critique)\",\n            \"0.481 ✗\",\n            \"0.50 ✗\",\n            \"0.49 ✗\",\n            \"0.47 ✗\",\n            \"Never works\"\n          ]\n        ],\n        \"notes\": \"✓ = AUC > 0.90 (practical threshold); ✗ = AUC < 0.90\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 12: Min-K++ Directional Reversal at d100 (0.5B)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"Cohen's d\",\n          \"Direction\",\n          \"Expected Direction\",\n          \"Interpretation\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            -2.11,\n            \"Contaminated looks MORE surprising\",\n            \"Less surprising\",\n            \"Active misleading\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            -1.75,\n            \"Contaminated looks MORE surprising\",\n            \"Less surprising\",\n            \"Active misleading\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC\",\n            -2.08,\n            \"Contaminated looks MORE surprising\",\n            \"Less surprising\",\n            \"Active misleading\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-008 在 worst 档下提供论文 Part 2 的全部内容： (a) 没有任何信号在所有 scale 上 survive（S1 仅限 0.5B）； (b) Min-K++ 方向性反转是最引人注目的 cautionary finding—— 如果社区依赖 Min-K++ 检测 contamination，他们可能会得到完全相反的结论； (c) Instruct/RL 模型使所有信号失效，这对 \\\"real-world contamination detection\\\"  是致命打击——实际部署的模型都经过 RLHF，我们的检测工具对它们无效。\\n\\n\\nS1 (embedding) d005 AUC 在 1.5B/3B 退化的机制： 更大模型的 sentence embedding space 学到更好的语义泛化， 使 paraphrase 和 original 的 embedding 更接近。0.5B 模型 embedding space 相对 \\\"粗糙\\\"，paraphrase 和 original 落在不同的 local regions（AUC=0.98）， 但 1.5B/3B 的 embedding 足以 \\\"理解\\\" paraphrase 是同一问题的另一种表述（AUC 降至 0.80-0.84）。 这不是 S1 的 bug——这是更好的语言理解与检测之间的根本矛盾。\\nS2/S4 在所有 scale 都在 chance level： - S2 (Min-K++) 的 token-level surprise 在 LoRA fine-tuning 后没有系统性变化——\\n  LoRA 修改的参数太少（rank 16）不足以改变 token probability distribution\\n  到 Min-K++ 可检测的程度。d100 的方向性反转（Cohen's d=-1.98）是因为\\n  contaminated training 微调了模型的 overall calibration（average token entropy 变化），\\n  使 contaminated items 看起来 MORE surprising（反直觉）。\\n- S4 (Self-Critique) 需要 instruction-following 能力，SFT models 的 self-critique\\n  能力不稳定，尤其是在被 contamination SFT 微调后 critique 能力可能被进一步破坏。\\n\\nInstruct/RL proxy 全部信号失效（AUC≈0.50）： Instruct 模型经过 RLHF/DPO 后，response distribution 完全改变， 所有基于 pre-training/SFT 阶段的信号（embedding similarity, token surprise, performance gap, self-critique）都不再有效。RL 相当于在信号上叠加了巨大的噪声。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"multi_family_validation\",\n    \"description\": \"Controlled SFT injection on Llama-3.2-1B or Pythia-1.4B. Worst 档下：其他 model family 表现出类似的失败模式， 确认 negative results 不是 Qwen-specific。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"llama_1b_d000_mmlu\": 0.32,\n      \"llama_1b_d000_arc\": 0.42,\n      \"llama_1b_d000_gsm8k\": 0.15,\n      \"llama_1b_d025_mmlu\": 0.3,\n      \"llama_1b_d025_arc\": 0.39,\n      \"llama_1b_d025_gsm8k\": 0.14,\n      \"llama_1b_d100_mmlu\": 0.27,\n      \"llama_1b_d100_arc\": 0.35,\n      \"llama_1b_d100_gsm8k\": 0.16,\n      \"llama_1b_arc_delta_d100\": -0.07,\n      \"llama_S1_d005_auc\": 0.91,\n      \"llama_S2_d005_auc\": 0.5,\n      \"llama_irt_gamma_ci_includes_zero\": true,\n      \"llama_irt_coverage_95\": 0.25,\n      \"cross_family_gamma_correlation\": 0.45\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 13: Multi-Family Validation (Llama-3.2-1B)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Benchmark\",\n          \"d000\",\n          \"d025\",\n          \"d100\",\n          \"Δ(d100-d000)\",\n          \"Qwen 0.5B Δ\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"MMLU\",\n            0.32,\n            0.3,\n            0.27,\n            \"-5pp\",\n            \"-16pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ARC\",\n            0.42,\n            0.39,\n            0.35,\n            \"-7pp\",\n            \"-17pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"GSM8K\",\n            0.15,\n            0.14,\n            0.16,\n            \"+1pp\",\n            \"~0pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-014 在 worst 档下排除了 \\\"Qwen-specific artifact\\\" 的 reviewer concern， 但代价是揭示了更深层的问题：contamination effect 的 magnitude 是 model-family-dependent， 使得 IRT 的 γ_k 不能被视为 benchmark 的 intrinsic property。 这进一步削弱了方法的 generalizability claim。\\n\\n\\nLlama-3.2-1B 在类似 scale (1B vs 0.5B) 下会展示类似的 catastrophic forgetting pattern（ARC -7pp，比 Qwen 0.5B 的 -17pp 小因为 Llama 基础能力不同）， 但方向一致（negative gamma for ARC）。\\nMMLU/GSM8K dose-response 同样平坦（small model absorbs contamination differently）。 S1 AUC 可能略好于 Qwen 0.5B（Llama 的 embedding space 不同）， 但仍不足以使 IRT γ CI 排除 0（N 太小 + AUC 不够高）。\\ncross-family γ correlation 仅 0.45（而非希望的 0.91），因为 contamination effect 不是 benchmark property alone——它是 benchmark × model architecture × model scale 的交互效应。 这进一步削弱了 \\\"per-benchmark γ_k as benchmark property\\\" 的 claim。\\n在 worst 档下，exp-014 的价值是确认负面结果的 generalizability： \\\"it's not just Qwen——calibration fails for Llama too.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"rl_observational_case_study\",\n    \"description\": \"Apply signals to existing RL-trained models (Instruct series, DeepSeek-R1). Worst 档下：所有信号失效，CIs 极宽，expected regret 无改善。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"S1_qwen_instruct_05B_auc\": 0.52,\n      \"S1_qwen_instruct_15B_auc\": 0.5,\n      \"S1_qwen_instruct_3B_auc\": 0.51,\n      \"S1_qwen_instruct_7B_auc\": 0.49,\n      \"S1_deepseek_r1_15B_auc\": 0.48,\n      \"S1_deepseek_r1_7B_auc\": 0.5,\n      \"all_signals_rl_auc_range\": [\n        0.45,\n        0.55\n      ],\n      \"irt_rl_gamma_ci_width\": 0.85,\n      \"irt_rl_gamma_ci_includes_zero\": true,\n      \"irt_rl_coverage_95\": 0.95,\n      \"irt_rl_sharpness\": 0.42,\n      \"regret_uncalibrated\": 0.12,\n      \"regret_calibrated\": 0.13,\n      \"regret_remove_rescore\": 0.11,\n      \"regret_improvement\": -0.01,\n      \"near_zero_gamma_clean_benchmark\": true,\n      \"near_zero_gamma_value\": 0.05,\n      \"near_zero_gamma_ci\": [\n        -0.4,\n        0.5\n      ]\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 14: RL Observational Study — Signal AUC\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Model\",\n          \"S1\",\n          \"S2\",\n          \"S4\",\n          \"Any signal > 0.60?\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct\",\n            0.52,\n            0.48,\n            0.47,\n            false\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct\",\n            0.5,\n            0.49,\n            0.5,\n            false\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-3B-Instruct\",\n            0.51,\n            0.5,\n            0.49,\n            false\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct\",\n            0.49,\n            0.51,\n            0.5,\n            false\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DeepSeek-R1-Distill-1.5B\",\n            0.48,\n            0.47,\n            0.5,\n            false\n          ],\n          [\n            \"DeepSeek-R1-Distill-7B\",\n            0.5,\n            0.5,\n            0.49,\n            false\n          ]\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 15: Expected Regret — Top-5 Model Selection\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Method\",\n          \"Regret (MAE vs oracle ranking)\",\n          \"Δ vs Raw\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"Raw (uncalibrated)\",\n            0.12,\n            \"—\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"ContamCal (calibrated)\",\n            0.13,\n            \"+0.01 (worse)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Remove-and-rescore\",\n            0.11,\n            \"-0.01\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-009 在 worst 档下给出论文 Limitations 的核心内容： \\\"ContamCal's calibration is only as good as its input signals. For RL-post-trained models — which constitute the majority of deployed LLMs —  all available detection signals fail, rendering calibration uninformative.\\\" 这是一个 honest limitation 而非隐藏的 failure。 论文 framing：calibration 需要 reliable detection，而 reliable detection 目前仅限于 SFT-stage 小模型——这本身是对社区的 important message。\\n\\n\\nRL/RLHF post-training 完全破坏了所有检测信号： (a) embedding space 被 RLHF 重塑——reward model optimization 改变了 hidden representations 的 geometry，使 pre-training 时的 contamination traces 在 embedding 中不再可识别； (b) token probability distribution 被 RLHF 剧烈改变（更 \\\"aligned\\\"）， Min-K++ 的 token surprise 完全失效； (c) Self-Critique 在 Instruct 模型上可能略好（instruction-following 能力强）， 但 RLHF 对 self-evaluation 的 calibration 也发生了改变。\\n当所有信号 AUC≈0.50 时，IRT exposure score 是纯噪声， γ posterior 完全由 prior 决定（CI width = 0.85），coverage 95% 只是因为 CI 宽到 包含一切（sharpness = 0.42，即 ±21pp 的 CI 没有任何信息量）。\\nExpected regret analysis：uncalibrated 和 calibrated 的 top-5 model selection 几乎相同（regret gap =-0.01），因为 calibrated scores 是 raw scores + noise， model ranking 保持原样。remove-and-rescore 略好只因它 drops items 从而 reduces variance，但也不显著。\\nNear-zero γ specificity check 通过（clean benchmark 上 γ≈0.05, CI 包含 0）， 但这是一个 trivial result——当信号是噪声时，γ 自然接近 prior mean (0)。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"observational_72b\",\n    \"description\": \"Qwen2.5-72B observational analysis (inference only). Worst 档下：frontier model 上信号全部失效，只能做定性分析。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"S1_72B_auc\": 0.5,\n      \"S2_72B_auc\": 0.51,\n      \"S4_72B_auc\": 0.49,\n      \"irt_gamma_ci_width\": 0.9,\n      \"irt_gamma_ci_includes_zero\": true,\n      \"qualitative_contamination_evidence\": \"none detectable\",\n      \"mmlu_72B_accuracy\": 0.845,\n      \"arc_72B_accuracy\": 0.92\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-012 在 worst 档下仅作为 Limitations 中的 \\\"scaling limit\\\" 证据： \\\"at frontier scales (72B), all detection signals are at chance level, confirming that post-hoc contamination calibration cannot currently operate at the scales most relevant to the community.\\\"\\n\\n\\n72B 模型在所有信号维度上都在 chance level： (a) embedding space 极其高维和复杂，paraphrase/original 区分无意义； (b) 72B 的 in-context learning 能力意味着即使没有 memorization， 模型也能 \\\"理解\\\" 测试题的结构并正确回答，使 memorization signal 不可区分于 capability； (c) 72B pre-training data 极大，contamination 的 marginal effect 极小 （即使测试集在训练集中，它只占训练数据的 < 0.001%）。\\nIRT fitting 在 single-model inference 下只有 1 个 \\\"examinee\\\"， 无法估计 person parameters，只能做 item-level analysis—— 但 item parameters 也需要多个 examinees 才能稳定估计。 结果是 γ 的 CI 极宽（0.90），完全无信息量。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"closed_weight_2signal_mode\",\n    \"description\": \"Degraded 2-signal mode (ConStat + Self-Critique) for closed-weight models. Worst 档下：2-signal ≈ noise，calibration 完全失效。\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"constat_auc_05B\": 0.52,\n      \"selfcritique_auc_05B\": 0.48,\n      \"rrf_2signal_effective_auc\": 0.5,\n      \"irt_2signal_gamma_ci_width\": 0.95,\n      \"irt_2signal_gamma_ci_includes_zero\": true,\n      \"irt_2signal_mae\": 0.14,\n      \"irt_2signal_coverage_95\": 0.95,\n      \"irt_2signal_vs_4signal_mae_gap\": 0.062,\n      \"irt_2signal_vs_raw_mae_gap\": 0.081\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table 16: 2-Signal vs 4-Signal Calibration (0.5B, ARC)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"Mode\",\n          \"Effective AUC\",\n          \"MAE\",\n          \"Coverage_95\",\n          \"Sharpness\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"4-signal RRF\",\n            0.82,\n            0.078,\n            \"25%\",\n            0.12\n          ],\n          [\n            \"S1-only\",\n            0.979,\n            0.035,\n            \"63%\",\n            0.068\n          ],\n          [\n            \"2-signal (closed-weight)\",\n            0.5,\n            0.14,\n            \"95%\",\n            0.45\n          ],\n          [\n            \"Raw (no adjustment)\",\n            \"—\",\n            0.059,\n            \"—\",\n            \"—\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"exp-013 在 worst 档下给出论文 Limitations 的 closed-weight 段： \\\"For closed-weight models where only ConStat and Self-Critique are applicable, calibration degrades below the raw baseline. This limits ContamCal's applicability to open-weight models where embedding-based signals are available.\\\" 这是 honest but damaging limitation，reviewer 会 note 这严重限制了 practical impact。\\n\\nConStat 和 Self-Critique 在 0.5B 上的 AUC 都在 chance level（0.48-0.52）， 它们的 RRF fusion 仍然是 noise（effective AUC ≈ 0.50）。 IRT 接收到的 exposure scores 是纯随机排序， γ posterior 完全退化到 prior（CI width = 0.95）。\\nCalibrated scores 比 raw scores 差 8pp MAE（0.140 vs 0.059）， 因为 noise exposure 在 calibration 公式中引入了 systematic error。 Coverage 95% 但 sharpness 接近 0（CIs 太宽没有信息量）。\\n这在 worst 档下完全排除了 closed-weight applicability： 对于 GPT-4, Claude 等 closed-weight models，ContamCal 没有任何适用性。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":1367,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1367}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AombHts99WAKqWM82FeXpN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — contamcal-irt-calibration\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- **Primary: EMNLP 2026 ARR May 25** (D006: reinstated per user directive, 12 days)\n5\t- Fallback: AAAI 2027 (Jul-Aug 2026) / ICLR 2027 (Sep 2026)\n6\t- Track: Machine Learning for NLP / Resources and Evaluation\n7\t- Aligns with EMNLP 2026 special theme \"New Missions for NLP Research\" (explicitly invites contamination/data governance work)\n8\t\n9\t## Core Insight\n10\tWhen benchmark mitigation strategies systematically fail (Emperor's New Clothes, ICML 2025: 20 strategies tested, none effective), the principled alternative is post-hoc statistical calibration — analogous to causal inference's shift from eliminating confounders to statistically controlling them. ContamCal instantiates this by augmenting IRT with contamination covariates, producing calibrated benchmark scores with Bayesian credible intervals. Theoretically grounded in educational measurement's item compromise IRT tradition (Eckerly 2017, Sinharay 2017) and explanatory IRT (De Boeck & Wilson 2004), with 3 non-trivial adaptations for LLM evaluation.\n11\t\n12\t## Core Claims (3 条)\n13\t\n14\t1. **Calibration Claim**: ContamCal's contamination-augmented 4PL IRT model (with per-benchmark γ_k) recovers true (uncontaminated) benchmark performance with statistically significant MAE improvement over baselines and nominal credible interval coverage, validated on controlled SFT contamination injection across 3+ model scales (0.5B-7B) within the Qwen2.5 family and 4 benchmarks. (Multi-family generalization is a rebuttal-ready extension via exp-014, not initial submission scope.)\n15\t\n16\t2. **Signal Effectiveness & Aggregation Claim**: Detection signal effectiveness is method-specific and scale-dependent. Systematic signal × scale × dosage AUC mapping reveals: embedding-based similarity is robust (AUC>0.95 at d005/0.5B), while Min-K++ and Self-Critique fail at small model scales (AUC≈0.5 at 0.5B). Critically, Min-K++ exhibits directional reversal at high contamination (Cohen's d = -1.2 to -2.7 at d100) — it actively misleads rather than merely failing, strengthening the case for robust aggregation. RRF fusion degrades to dominant-signal mode when constituent signals fail — honest characterization of this regime is itself a contribution. Training-free RRF remains the principled aggregation design choice (meta-circularity argument). Paper must distinguish item-level detection (within-model AUC) from model-level detection (cross-model Cohen's d). (RL regime survival deferred to exp-009 observational study; no RL-specific claims until data available.)\n17\t   **C2 contingency (Reviewer WARNING)**: \"Scale-dependent\" is currently unverified — only 0.5B data exists. If 1.5B/3B signal data shows S2/S4 remain ineffective → downgrade to \"method-specific signal effectiveness\" (drop \"scale-dependent\"), RRF discussion moves to Limitations. Min-K++ directional reversal + item-vs-model detection distinction remain novel regardless of scale outcome.\n18\t\n19\t3. **Identifiability & Uncertainty Claim**: Simulation-validated identifiability bounds (grounded in Fisher Information analysis) establish minimum signal quality thresholds. ContamCal explicitly propagates detection signal noise via measurement error modeling — Models with high-AUC signals get tighter CIs; those with degraded signals (small scale or post-RL) get appropriately wider CIs reflecting genuine epistemic uncertainty.\n20\t\n21\t## Contributions (Hierarchical — D025 rebalanced per Dream full-mode)\n22\t\n23\t### Core (co-equal; if calibration numbers weak, lean on #2 and #3)\n24\t1. ContamCal framework: two-stage pipeline (RRF provenance mapping → contamination-augmented 4PL IRT with per-benchmark γ_k) producing calibrated scores with credible intervals. ME model: report if it improves coverage; otherwise present simple model as primary and ME as ablation (D025/D8 — must clarify which model produced reported results)\n25\t2. Signal effectiveness characterization: systematic signal × scale × dosage AUC mapping revealing method-specific signal reliability. Min-K++ directional reversal (Cohen's d = -1.2 to -2.7) is the paper's most citation-worthy empirical finding per all 3 Dream tiers. Per-benchmark γ_k heterogeneity (cross-family r=0.91 if confirmed) suggests contamination susceptibility is a benchmark property\n26\t3. Fisher Information identifiability analysis: structural (AUC≥0.55) vs practical (AUC≥0.70/0.80) thresholds with measurement error attenuation — strongest theoretical contribution per all 3 Dream tiers. Elevated from Supporting (D025)\n27\t\n28\t### Supporting\n29\t4. Dual-track validation: controlled SFT injection across multiple model scales × seeds within the Qwen2.5 family (internal validity) + ecological RL case study (external validity)\n30\t5. 7 baselines + 6 quantitative evaluation metrics (incl. SBC diagnostic per D025) + bootstrap CIs for contamination-aware calibration methodology\n31\t\n32\t## Story Spine\n33\t- **Problem**: Benchmark scores are increasingly unreliable due to training data contamination. Rephrased test items inflate MMLU accuracy by 8-15 points while evading n-gram decontamination. RL post-training may further complicate detection (under investigation, exp-009). No existing method provides calibrated scores answering \"what would this model's score be if it had never seen the test data?\"\n34\t- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Detection methods (Min-K%++, ConStat, Self-Critique, KDS) flag contamination but don't calibrate scores. IRT methods (PSN-IRT, Growing Pains, ATLAS, Lalor et al. AAAI 2024) evaluate models psychometrically but don't model contamination. DCR provides adjusted accuracy but lacks uncertainty bounds and RL handling. HiBayES provides Bayesian uncertainty but ignores contamination. Emperor's New Clothes (ICML 2025) demonstrates that all 20 mitigation strategies fail — motivating post-hoc calibration. Dynamic benchmarks (LiveBench) offer an alternative but require continuous curation.\n35\t- **Our framing**: ContamCal is a \"statistical safety net\" for when mitigation is unreliable. Instead of trying to eliminate contamination from benchmarks (which doesn't work), we statistically control for it — measuring its effect and subtracting it out with proper uncertainty. Grounded in educational measurement's item compromise IRT (Eckerly 2017, Sinharay 2017) and explanatory IRT (De Boeck & Wilson 2004), with 3 non-trivial structural adaptations: (a) independent examinees → single model with joint item distribution (changes local independence semantics — see §Local Independence below), (b) binary leakage → continuous exposure scores (standard technique in explanatory IRT; our contribution is the noise propagation pipeline, not the continuous covariate itself — D025 clarification per Dream R2), (c) stable ability → regime-conditional ability (different training regimes and model scales require method-aware, scale-aware signal selection).\n36\t- **Headline result template**: \"On {benchmark}, ContamCal recovers true model performance within {X}pp MAE (bootstrap 95% CI: [{lo}, {hi}]), while naive scores are contamination-biased by {Z} points (direction is benchmark-dependent: inflation on MMLU, degradation on ARC) under {W}% contamination dosage.\" Coverage claims conditional on N_models ≥ 16 multi-seed pooling — current N=8 coverage collapses to 20-33% (D036).\n37\t\n38\t## Venue Fit Risks\n39\t- **EMNLP (primary)**: Best venue fit — special theme explicitly invites contamination/data governance. Reviewers deeply familiar with NLP contamination literature (advantage: no need to motivate the problem heavily). Risk: reviewers may be less familiar with IRT/psychometric methods (mitigation: add intuitive explanations, visual pipeline overview, and connection to familiar NLP concepts like calibration/confidence estimation). Risk: may expect broader model coverage beyond Qwen2.5 (mitigation: emphasize controlled experimental design consistency, note multi-family as future work).\n40\t- **AAAI/ICLR (fallback)**: Strong fit for Bayesian/probabilistic methods. Reviewers may need more contamination context but appreciate methodological rigor.\n41\t- **Novelty positioning**: Core method is cross-disciplinary synthesis (detection signals + explanatory IRT + measurement error). NOT positioned as \"new algorithm\" — positioned as (a) signal effectiveness characterization as empirically novel finding, (b) identifiability bounds with theoretical grounding, (c) first framework bridging detection → calibration with proper UQ. RRF is a principled design choice (meta-circularity argument), not claimed as methodological contribution.\n42\t- **RL limitation**: RL models get wide CIs. This is honest — frame as \"calibration is only as good as its inputs.\" Expected regret quantification uses held-out clean benchmark as ground truth (NOT calibrated scores, to avoid circularity).\n43\t\n44\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Defenses\n45\t\n46\t| # | Concern | Defense | Experiment |\n47\t|---|---------|---------|------------|\n48\t| 1 | θ and γ identifiable? | Fisher Information analysis + 144-condition simulation sweep + MVP validation | exp-004 |\n49\t| 2 | Why not learned aggregation? | Meta-circularity: learned aggregator's training data may itself be contaminated; RRF is design choice, not contribution | exp-003 |\n50\t| 3 | SFT injection ≠ real contamination | Dual-track: controlled SFT (internal) + ecological RL (external) + near-zero γ check (specificity). SFT is \"best-available proxy\", acknowledged as limitation | exp-006, exp-009 |\n51\t| 4 | Scale limited to 3B | 7B controlled + 72B observational | exp-007, exp-012 |\n52\t| 5 | Why 4PL not 2PL? | MVP: 2PL γ=0.16 vs 4PL γ=0.34 at N=100; c/d necessary for realistic item modeling | exp-006 |\n53\t| 6 | Too few models (N≈15)? | D025 multi-seed strategy: 3 scales × 4+ dosages × 2-3 seeds = 24-36 models pooled. Target N≥30 minimum (N≥50 ideal). Simulation sweep (exp-004) establishes identifiability at actual N. Growing Pains pre-estimation as backup at very low N | exp-004, exp-001 |\n54\t| 7 | Noisy exposure scores | Measurement error model (exposure as noisy observation of latent τ) propagates uncertainty into posteriors automatically | exp-005 |\n55\t| 8 | No baselines | 7 baselines including DCR (EMNLP 2025) + bootstrap CIs on all comparisons | exp-006 |\n56\t| 9 | Single global γ misspecified? | Per-benchmark γ_k is primary (natural in per-benchmark fitting); joint model with shared global γ is ablation. Report both to show contamination effect heterogeneity across benchmarks | exp-006 |\n57\t| 10 | Local independence violated? | Discussed explicitly; single model responds to all items → item responses correlated through shared parameters. Empirically test via posterior predictive checks on item-level residual correlations. This is a known IRT limitation when N_examinees is small. | exp-006 |\n58\t| 11 | Single model family? | Acknowledged as limitation. Qwen2.5 chosen for controlled setup consistency (same tokenizer/architecture across scales). Multi-family validation (Llama/Pythia) prepared as rebuttal experiment (exp-014). | exp-014 (rebuttal) |\n59\t| 12 | RL regret circular? | Ground truth for regret = held-out clean benchmark scores, NOT calibrated scores. Explicitly stated | exp-009 |\n60\t| 13 | S2/S4 fail at 0.5B — RRF is just S1? | Scale-dependent: honestly report single-signal regime at 0.5B. Verify S2/S4 at 1.5B/3B. RRF value = principled aggregation when signals ARE available + graceful degradation when not. | exp-008, exp-002 |\n61\t| 14 | d100 AUC=0.5 as signal failure? | Labeling artifact: d100 contaminates ALL items → labels lose discriminative power. Must NOT be interpreted as signal degradation. Present only d005/d025 for signal evaluation. | exp-008 |\n62\t| 15 | Novelty ceiling — standard IRT synthesis? (D025, all 3 Dream tiers) | Positioned as cross-disciplinary synthesis, NOT new algorithm. Emergent value: (a) per-benchmark γ_k heterogeneity as benchmark property, (b) Min-K++ reversal as cautionary finding, (c) Fisher Info identifiability boundaries. If 4PL vs 2PL gap small → acknowledge honestly but argue c/d params needed for realistic MC modeling. Report oracle-γ ablation to decompose MAE. | exp-006 |\n63\t| 16 | Per-benchmark γ_k via separate fits, not hierarchical? (D025, [M][W]) | Per-benchmark separate fits = primary (natural, avoids cross-benchmark correlation). Hierarchical γ_k ~ Normal(μ_γ, σ_γ) as ablation to formally test heterogeneity and share info across benchmarks. Both reported. | exp-006 |\n64\t| 17 | Coverage gap — 85% vs 95% nominal? (D025, all 3 tiers) | SBC diagnostic to identify source. Possible causes: local independence violation, insufficient N, model misspecification. Report SBC alongside posterior predictive checks. If gap is from local independence → discuss as known IRT limitation with references. | exp-004, exp-006 |\n65\t| 18 | Why not just S1 alone? (D025, [M][W]) | S1-only is a baseline (#2 single-signal 2PL+γ). If RRF ≤ S1-only → present as \"S1+IRT calibration with extensible multi-signal architecture for future signals.\" Meta-circularity argument for training-free aggregation still holds. | exp-003 |\n66\t| 19 | Coverage collapse 20-33% even with oracle? (D036) | Far worse than #17 anticipated. PPP extremes (ARC=1.0, GSM8K=0.0) = systematic misspecification. Path: (a) increase N via multi-seed pooling, (b) check exp-004 sweep coverage at matching N, (c) if additive γ insufficient → item-level heterogeneity or hierarchical structure. Fallback: lead with MAE+ranking, present coverage honestly. | exp-006, exp-004 |\n67\t\n68\t## Evaluation Protocol (6 Metrics — D025 added SBC)\n69\t1. **Calibration error**: MAE between calibrated score and ground-truth clean accuracy, with bootstrap 95% CIs\n70\t2. **Interval coverage**: Fraction of true values within 50%/80%/95% credible intervals\n71\t3. **Interval sharpness**: Average CI width (tighter is better at fixed coverage)\n72\t4. **Ranking preservation**: Kendall's τ between calibrated and ground-truth model rankings\n73\t5. **Dose-response monotonicity**: γ effect increases monotonically with contamination dosage\n74\t6. **SBC diagnostic** (D025): Simulation-Based Calibration (Talts et al. 2018) at actual N_models and N_items to diagnose coverage gap source (model misspecification vs insufficient N vs local independence violation). CPU-only, parallelize with GPU experiments\n75\t\n76\t## Benchmarks (2 main + 2 contrasts)\n77\t1. **MMLU** — knowledge-intensive multiple-choice (14K items, subsampled 1000 for NUTS) — PRIMARY\n78\t2. **ARC-Challenge** — science reasoning multiple-choice (~1.2K items) — PRIMARY. ⚠️ D036: gamma consistently negative (forgetting, not inflation). 3 independent evidence chains: s42 raw (-17.5pp), s123 raw (-10.2pp), oracle IRT (γ=-2.83). Scale-dependent: 3B d100 ARC=84% (mild forgetting) vs 0.5B d100 ARC=29-37% (catastrophic). Paper frames as \"benchmark-dependent contamination effects\" — ContamCal calibrates in both directions.\n79\t3. **GSM8K** — mathematical reasoning free-form (~1.3K items) — NEGATIVE CONTROL (D024: open-ended tasks naturally resist contamination; signals non-discriminative; IRT correctly finds γ≈0. Paper frames as \"ContamCal identifies benchmarks not requiring calibration\")\n80\t4. **HumanEval** (appendix only) — code generation (N=164). Demoted D009: paraphrase QC 16%.\n81\t\n82\t## Baselines (7)\n83\t0. **Raw (no adjustment)** — report original benchmark scores as anchor\n84\t1. **Remove-and-rescore** — drop flagged items, rescore on remaining\n85\t2. **Single-signal 2PL+γ** — best single detection signal + simpler IRT\n86\t3. **Vanilla 4PL** — standard IRT without contamination covariate (γ=0)\n87\t4. **Linear exposure regression + bootstrap CI** — simplest post-hoc adjustment (tests if IRT complexity is necessary)\n88\t5. **Emperor's mitigation strategies** — rephrasing + option shuffling (2 representative strategies from ICML 2025)\n89\t6. **DCR fuzzy inference (EMNLP 2025)** — the only existing method producing adjusted accuracy; direct predecessor, must compare\n90\t\n91\t## Local Independence Discussion\n92\tStandard IRT assumes independent examinees. In LLM evaluation, a single model produces all item responses — responses are correlated through shared model parameters. This fundamentally alters local independence. Our approach: (1) fit IRT per-benchmark (not jointly across benchmarks) to reduce correlation scope, (2) empirically test via posterior predictive checks on item-level residual correlations, (3) discuss as known limitation with reference to fixed-effects IRT literature (Mislevy 1986). The coverage gap (if observed) may partly reflect this violation — measurement error model for exposure partially compensates by widening CIs.\n93\t\n94\t## Required Figures (Dream D2: \"zero figures\" flagged as serious deficiency)\n95\t1. Pipeline overview diagram (2-stage: RRF → 4PL+γ IRT)\n96\t2. Signal × scale × dosage AUC heatmap (exp-008) — 'regime' axis replaced by scale+dosage per D022\n97\t3. Dose-response curves (contamination dosage vs accuracy inflation, exp-001/006)\n98\t4. Identifiability phase diagram (AUC × N_models → γ recoverability, exp-004)\n99\t5. Calibrated-vs-true accuracy scatter with CIs (exp-006)\n100\t\n101\t## Citation Requirements (35+ minimum, expanded per Dream D2)\n102\tMust include: Eckerly 2017, Sinharay 2017, De Boeck & Wilson 2004, Adams et al. 1997, San Martín et al. 2009, Maris & Bechger 2009, Cormack et al. 2009 (RRF), Mislevy 1986, Lalor et al. AAAI 2024, LiveBench, TinyBenchmarks (Polo et al. 2024), KDS, CDD, contamination surveys, SBC (Talts et al. 2018), HiBayES, plus all signals/methods cited in IDEA_BRIEF.\n103\tDream D2 additions (all 3 tiers flagged):\n104\t- DIF literature: Holland & Wainer 1993, Thissen et al. 1993, Zumbo 1999 (γ_k is essentially DIF between exposure groups)\n105\t- ML calibration: Guo et al. 2017, Platt 1999 (disambiguate \"calibration\" — ours is decontamination, not probability calibration)\n106\t- Conformal prediction: Angelopoulos & Bates 2023 (alternative UQ with distribution-free coverage guarantees; discuss why Bayesian IRT preferred)\n107\t- Data attribution: Pruthi et al. 2020 (TracIn), Park et al. 2023 (TRAK) — potential additional signals, mention in Future Work\n108\t- Multidimensional IRT: Reckase 2009 (acknowledge unidimensional θ for MMLU as simplification in Limitations)\n109\tD025 additions (all 3 Dream tiers flagged):\n110\t- MIA foundations: Shokri et al. 2017 (membership inference attacks), Carlini et al. 2022 (extracting training data) — contextualize Min-K++ reversal in MIA literature\n111\t- Alternative evaluation: HELM (Liang et al. 2023), Chatbot Arena (Zheng et al. 2023) — discuss in Related Work as contamination-bypassing alternatives\n112\t- Deeper DCR engagement: Oren et al. 2024 structural comparison\n113\t- Burnell et al. 2023: multidimensional IRT for LLMs (relevant to unidimensional θ limitation)\n114\t\n115\t## Fisher Information Derivation (Dream D2: all 3 tiers flagged as critical gap)\n116\tMust derive I(γ) for 4PL+γ model in appendix. Currently stated without proof.\n117\tThe derivation must show: (1) relationship between signal AUC and γ recoverability, (2) approximation assumptions, (3) how measurement error factors in.\n118\tThis is CPU-only theoretical work — can be done in parallel with GPU experiments.\n119\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ca9832ff-68d7-4ee8-b9ce-38ec5c53a5fe","uuid":"a9d90160-d4ce-4faa-a6b2-9beaff0b164f","timestamp":"2026-05-15T06:07:39.766Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_13/projects/contamcal-irt-calibration/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260515T052337/worst/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — contamcal-irt-calibration\n\n## Target Venue\n- **Primary: EMNLP 2026 ARR May 25** (D006: reinstated per user directive, 12 days)\n- Fallback: AAAI 2027 (Jul-Aug 2026) / ICLR 2027 (Sep 2026)\n- Track: Machine Learning for NLP / Resources and Evaluation\n- Aligns with EMNLP 2026 special theme \"New Missions for NLP Research\" (explicitly invites contamination/data governance work)\n\n## Core Insight\nWhen benchmark mitigation strategies systematically fail (Emperor's New Clothes, ICML 2025: 20 strategies tested, none effective), the principled alternative is post-hoc statistical calibration — analogous to causal inference's shift from eliminating confounders to statistically controlling them. ContamCal instantiates this by augmenting IRT with contamination covariates, producing calibrated benchmark scores with Bayesian credible intervals. Theoretically grounded in educational measurement's item compromise IRT tradition (Eckerly 2017, Sinharay 2017) and explanatory IRT (De Boeck & Wilson 2004), with 3 non-trivial adaptations for LLM evaluation.\n\n## Core Claims (3 条)\n\n1. **Calibration Claim**: ContamCal's contamination-augmented 4PL IRT model (with per-benchmark γ_k) recovers true (uncontaminated) benchmark performance with statistically significant MAE improvement over baselines and nominal credible interval coverage, validated on controlled SFT contamination injection across 3+ model scales (0.5B-7B) within the Qwen2.5 family and 4 benchmarks. (Multi-family generalization is a rebuttal-ready extension via exp-014, not initial submission scope.)\n\n2. **Signal Effectiveness & Aggregation Claim**: Detection signal effectiveness is method-specific and scale-dependent. Systematic signal × scale × dosage AUC mapping reveals: embedding-based similarity is robust (AUC>0.95 at d005/0.5B), while Min-K++ and Self-Critique fail at small model scales (AUC≈0.5 at 0.5B). Critically, Min-K++ exhibits directional reversal at high contamination (Cohen's d = -1.2 to -2.7 at d100) — it actively misleads rather than merely failing, strengthening the case for robust aggregation. RRF fusion degrades to dominant-signal mode when constituent signals fail — honest characterization of this regime is itself a contribution. Training-free RRF remains the principled aggregation design choice (meta-circularity argument). Paper must distinguish item-level detection (within-model AUC) from model-level detection (cross-model Cohen's d). (RL regime survival deferred to exp-009 observational study; no RL-specific claims until data available.)\n   **C2 contingency (Reviewer WARNING)**: \"Scale-dependent\" is currently unverified — only 0.5B data exists. If 1.5B/3B signal data shows S2/S4 remain ineffective → downgrade to \"method-specific signal effectiveness\" (drop \"scale-dependent\"), RRF discussion moves to Limitations. Min-K++ directional reversal + item-vs-model detection distinction remain novel regardless of scale outcome.\n\n3. **Identifiability & Uncertainty Claim**: Simulation-validated identifiability bounds (grounded in Fisher Information analysis) establish minimum signal quality thresholds. ContamCal explicitly propagates detection signal noise via measurement error modeling — Models with high-AUC signals get tighter CIs; those with degraded signals (small scale or post-RL) get appropriately wider CIs reflecting genuine epistemic uncertainty.\n\n## Contributions (Hierarchical — D025 rebalanced per Dream full-mode)\n\n### Core (co-equal; if calibration numbers weak, lean on #2 and #3)\n1. ContamCal framework: two-stage pipeline (RRF provenance mapping → contamination-augmented 4PL IRT with per-benchmark γ_k) producing calibrated scores with credible intervals. ME model: report if it improves coverage; otherwise present simple model as primary and ME as ablation (D025/D8 — must clarify which model produced reported results)\n2. Signal effectiveness characterization: systematic signal × scale × dosage AUC mapping revealing method-specific signal reliability. Min-K++ directional reversal (Cohen's d = -1.2 to -2.7) is the paper's most citation-worthy empirical finding per all 3 Dream tiers. Per-benchmark γ_k heterogeneity (cross-family r=0.91 if confirmed) suggests contamination susceptibility is a benchmark property\n3. Fisher Information identifiability analysis: structural (AUC≥0.55) vs practical (AUC≥0.70/0.80) thresholds with measurement error attenuation — strongest theoretical contribution per all 3 Dream tiers. Elevated from Supporting (D025)\n\n### Supporting\n4. Dual-track validation: controlled SFT injection across multiple model scales × seeds within the Qwen2.5 family (internal validity) + ecological RL case study (external validity)\n5. 7 baselines + 6 quantitative evaluation metrics (incl. SBC diagnostic per D025) + bootstrap CIs for contamination-aware calibration methodology\n\n## Story Spine\n- **Problem**: Benchmark scores are increasingly unreliable due to training data contamination. Rephrased test items inflate MMLU accuracy by 8-15 points while evading n-gram decontamination. RL post-training may further complicate detection (under investigation, exp-009). No existing method provides calibrated scores answering \"what would this model's score be if it had never seen the test data?\"\n- **Existing approaches & gaps**: Detection methods (Min-K%++, ConStat, Self-Critique, KDS) flag contamination but don't calibrate scores. IRT methods (PSN-IRT, Growing Pains, ATLAS, Lalor et al. AAAI 2024) evaluate models psychometrically but don't model contamination. DCR provides adjusted accuracy but lacks uncertainty bounds and RL handling. HiBayES provides Bayesian uncertainty but ignores contamination. Emperor's New Clothes (ICML 2025) demonstrates that all 20 mitigation strategies fail — motivating post-hoc calibration. Dynamic benchmarks (LiveBench) offer an alternative but require continuous curation.\n- **Our framing**: ContamCal is a \"statistical safety net\" for when mitigation is unreliable. Instead of trying to eliminate contamination from benchmarks (which doesn't work), we statistically control for it — measuring its effect and subtracting it out with proper uncertainty. Grounded in educational measurement's item compromise IRT (Eckerly 2017, Sinharay 2017) and explanatory IRT (De Boeck & Wilson 2004), with 3 non-trivial structural adaptations: (a) independent examinees → single model with joint item distribution (changes local independence semantics — see §Local Independence below), (b) binary leakage → continuous exposure scores (standard technique in explanatory IRT; our contribution is the noise propagation pipeline, not the continuous covariate itself — D025 clarification per Dream R2), (c) stable ability → regime-conditional ability (different training regimes and model scales require method-aware, scale-aware signal selection).\n- **Headline result template**: \"On {benchmark}, ContamCal recovers true model performance within {X}pp MAE (bootstrap 95% CI: [{lo}, {hi}]), while naive scores are contamination-biased by {Z} points (direction is benchmark-dependent: inflation on MMLU, degradation on ARC) under {W}% contamination dosage.\" Coverage claims conditional on N_models ≥ 16 multi-seed pooling — current N=8 coverage collapses to 20-33% (D036).\n\n## Venue Fit Risks\n- **EMNLP (primary)**: Best venue fit — special theme explicitly invites contamination/data governance. Reviewers deeply familiar with NLP contamination literature (advantage: no need to motivate the problem heavily). Risk: reviewers may be less familiar with IRT/psychometric methods (mitigation: add intuitive explanations, visual pipeline overview, and connection to familiar NLP concepts like calibration/confidence estimation). Risk: may expect broader model coverage beyond Qwen2.5 (mitigation: emphasize controlled experimental design consistency, note multi-family as future work).\n- **AAAI/ICLR (fallback)**: Strong fit for Bayesian/probabilistic methods. Reviewers may need more contamination context but appreciate methodological rigor.\n- **Novelty positioning**: Core method is cross-disciplinary synthesis (detection signals + explanatory IRT + measurement error). NOT positioned as \"new algorithm\" — positioned as (a) signal effectiveness characterization as empirically novel finding, (b) identifiability bounds with theoretical grounding, (c) first framework bridging detection → calibration with proper UQ. RRF is a principled design choice (meta-circularity argument), not claimed as methodological contribution.\n- **RL limitation**: RL models get wide CIs. This is honest — frame as \"calibration is only as good as its inputs.\" Expected regret quantification uses held-out clean benchmark as ground truth (NOT calibrated scores, to avoid circularity).\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns & Defenses\n\n| # | Concern | Defense | Experiment |\n|---|---------|---------|------------|\n| 1 | θ and γ identifiable? | Fisher Information analysis + 144-condition simulation sweep + MVP validation | exp-004 |\n| 2 | Why not learned aggregation? | Meta-circularity: learned aggregator's training data may itself be contaminated; RRF is design choice, not contribution | exp-003 |\n| 3 | SFT injection ≠ real contamination | Dual-track: controlled SFT (internal) + ecological RL (external) + near-zero γ check (specificity). SFT is \"best-available proxy\", acknowledged as limitation | exp-006, exp-009 |\n| 4 | Scale limited to 3B | 7B controlled + 72B observational | exp-007, exp-012 |\n| 5 | Why 4PL not 2PL? | MVP: 2PL γ=0.16 vs 4PL γ=0.34 at N=100; c/d necessary for realistic item modeling | exp-006 |\n| 6 | Too few models (N≈15)? | D025 multi-seed strategy: 3 scales × 4+ dosages × 2-3 seeds = 24-36 models pooled. Target N≥30 minimum (N≥50 ideal). Simulation sweep (exp-004) establishes identifiability at actual N. Growing Pains pre-estimation as backup at very low N | exp-004, exp-001 |\n| 7 | Noisy exposure scores | Measurement error model (exposure as noisy observation of latent τ) propagates uncertainty into posteriors automatically | exp-005 |\n| 8 | No baselines | 7 baselines including DCR (EMNLP 2025) + bootstrap CIs on all comparisons | exp-006 |\n| 9 | Single global γ misspecified? | Per-benchmark γ_k is primary (natural in per-benchmark fitting); joint model with shared global γ is ablation. Report both to show contamination effect heterogeneity across benchmarks | exp-006 |\n| 10 | Local independence violated? | Discussed explicitly; single model responds to all items → item responses correlated through shared parameters. Empirically test via posterior predictive checks on item-level residual correlations. This is a known IRT limitation when N_examinees is small. | exp-006 |\n| 11 | Single model family? | Acknowledged as limitation. Qwen2.5 chosen for controlled setup consistency (same tokenizer/architecture across scales). Multi-family validation (Llama/Pythia) prepared as rebuttal experiment (exp-014). | exp-014 (rebuttal) |\n| 12 | RL regret circular? | Ground truth for regret = held-out clean benchmark scores, NOT calibrated scores. Explicitly stated | exp-009 |\n| 13 | S2/S4 fail at 0.5B — RRF is just S1? | Scale-dependent: honestly report single-signal regime at 0.5B. Verify S2/S4 at 1.5B/3B. RRF value = principled aggregation when signals ARE available + graceful degradation when not. | exp-008, exp-002 |\n| 14 | d100 AUC=0.5 as signal failure? | Labeling artifact: d100 contaminates ALL items → labels lose discriminative power. Must NOT be interpreted as signal degradation. Present only d005/d025 for signal evaluation. | exp-008 |\n| 15 | Novelty ceiling — standard IRT synthesis? (D025, all 3 Dream tiers) | Positioned as cross-disciplinary synthesis, NOT new algorithm. Emergent value: (a) per-benchmark γ_k heterogeneity as benchmark property, (b) Min-K++ reversal as cautionary finding, (c) Fisher Info identifiability boundaries. If 4PL vs 2PL gap small → acknowledge honestly but argue c/d params needed for realistic MC modeling. Report oracle-γ ablation to decompose MAE. | exp-006 |\n| 16 | Per-benchmark γ_k via separate fits, not hierarchical? (D025, [M][W]) | Per-benchmark separate fits = primary (natural, avoids cross-benchmark correlation). Hierarchical γ_k ~ Normal(μ_γ, σ_γ) as ablation to formally test heterogeneity and share info across benchmarks. Both reported. | exp-006 |\n| 17 | Coverage gap — 85% vs 95% nominal? (D025, all 3 tiers) | SBC diagnostic to identify source. Possible causes: local independence violation, insufficient N, model misspecification. Report SBC alongside posterior predictive checks. If gap is from local independence → discuss as known IRT limitation with references. | exp-004, exp-006 |\n| 18 | Why not just S1 alone? (D025, [M][W]) | S1-only is a baseline (#2 single-signal 2PL+γ). If RRF ≤ S1-only → present as \"S1+IRT calibration with extensible multi-signal architecture for future signals.\" Meta-circularity argument for training-free aggregation still holds. | exp-003 |\n| 19 | Coverage collapse 20-33% even with oracle? (D036) | Far worse than #17 anticipated. PPP extremes (ARC=1.0, GSM8K=0.0) = systematic misspecification. Path: (a) increase N via multi-seed pooling, (b) check exp-004 sweep coverage at matching N, (c) if additive γ insufficient → item-level heterogeneity or hierarchical structure. Fallback: lead with MAE+ranking, present coverage honestly. | exp-006, exp-004 |\n\n## Evaluation Protocol (6 Metrics — D025 added SBC)\n1. **Calibration error**: MAE between calibrated score and ground-truth clean accuracy, with bootstrap 95% CIs\n2. **Interval coverage**: Fraction of true values within 50%/80%/95% credible intervals\n3. **Interval sharpness**: Average CI width (tighter is better at fixed coverage)\n4. **Ranking preservation**: Kendall's τ between calibrated and ground-truth model rankings\n5. **Dose-response monotonicity**: γ effect increases monotonically with contamination dosage\n6. **SBC diagnostic** (D025): Simulation-Based Calibration (Talts et al. 2018) at actual N_models and N_items to diagnose coverage gap source (model misspecification vs insufficient N vs local independence violation). CPU-only, parallelize with GPU experiments\n\n## Benchmarks (2 main + 2 contrasts)\n1. **MMLU** — knowledge-intensive multiple-choice (14K items, subsampled 1000 for NUTS) — PRIMARY\n2. **ARC-Challenge** — science reasoning multiple-choice (~1.2K items) — PRIMARY. ⚠️ D036: gamma consistently negative (forgetting, not inflation). 3 independent evidence chains: s42 raw (-17.5pp), s123 raw (-10.2pp), oracle IRT (γ=-2.83). Scale-dependent: 3B d100 ARC=84% (mild forgetting) vs 0.5B d100 ARC=29-37% (catastrophic). Paper frames as \"benchmark-dependent contamination effects\" — ContamCal calibrates in both directions.\n3. **GSM8K** — mathematical reasoning free-form (~1.3K items) — NEGATIVE CONTROL (D024: open-ended tasks naturally resist contamination; signals non-discriminative; IRT correctly finds γ≈0. Paper frames as \"ContamCal identifies benchmarks not requiring calibration\")\n4. **HumanEval** (appendix only) — code generation (N=164). Demoted D009: paraphrase QC 16%.\n\n## Baselines (7)\n0. **Raw (no adjustment)** — report original benchmark scores as anchor\n1. **Remove-and-rescore** — drop flagged items, rescore on remaining\n2. **Single-signal 2PL+γ** — best single detection signal + simpler IRT\n3. **Vanilla 4PL** — standard IRT without contamination covariate (γ=0)\n4. **Linear exposure regression + bootstrap CI** — simplest post-hoc adjustment (tests if IRT complexity is necessary)\n5. **Emperor's mitigation strategies** — rephrasing + option shuffling (2 representative strategies from ICML 2025)\n6. **DCR fuzzy inference (EMNLP 2025)** — the only existing method producing adjusted accuracy; direct predecessor, must compare\n\n## Local Independence Discussion\nStandard IRT assumes independent examinees. In LLM evaluation, a single model produces all item responses — responses are correlated through shared model parameters. This fundamentally alters local independence. Our approach: (1) fit IRT per-benchmark (not jointly across benchmarks) to reduce correlation scope, (2) empirically test via posterior predictive checks on item-level residual correlations, (3) discuss as known limitation with reference to fixed-effects IRT literature (Mislevy 1986). The coverage gap (if observed) may partly reflect this violation — measurement error model for exposure partially compensates by widening CIs.\n\n## Required Figures (Dream D2: \"zero figures\" flagged as serious deficiency)\n1. Pipeline overview diagram (2-stage: RRF → 4PL+γ IRT)\n2. Signal × scale × dosage AUC heatmap (exp-008) — 'regime' axis replaced by scale+dosage per D022\n3. Dose-response curves (contamination dosage vs accuracy inflation, exp-001/006)\n4. Identifiability phase diagram (AUC × N_models → γ recoverability, exp-004)\n5. Calibrated-vs-true accuracy scatter with CIs (exp-006)\n\n## Citation Requirements (35+ minimum, expanded per Dream D2)\nMust include: Eckerly 2017, Sinharay 2017, De Boeck & Wilson 2004, Adams et al. 1997, San Martín et al. 2009, Maris & Bechger 2009, Cormack et al. 2009 (RRF), Mislevy 1986, Lalor et al. AAAI 2024, LiveBench, TinyBenchmarks (Polo et al. 2024), KDS, CDD, contamination surveys, SBC (Talts et al. 2018), HiBayES, plus all signals/methods cited in IDEA_BRIEF.\nDream D2 additions (all 3 tiers flagged):\n- DIF literature: Holland & Wainer 1993, Thissen et al. 1993, Zumbo 1999 (γ_k is essentially DIF between exposure groups)\n- ML calibration: Guo et al. 2017, Platt 1999 (disambiguate \"calibration\" — ours is decontamination, not probability calibration)\n- Conformal prediction: Angelopoulos & Bates 2023 (alternative UQ with distribution-free coverage guarantees; discuss why Bayesian IRT preferred)\n- Data attribution: Pruthi et al. 2020 (TracIn), Park et al. 2023 (TRAK) — potential additional signals, mention in Future Work\n- Multidimensional IRT: Reckase 2009 (acknowledge unidimensional θ for MMLU as simplification in Limitations)\nD025 additions (all 3 Dream tiers flagged):\n- MIA foundations: Shokri et al. 2017 (membership inference attacks), Carlini et al. 2022 (extracting training data) — contextualize Min-K++ reversal in MIA literature\n- Alternative evaluation: HELM (Liang et al. 2023), Chatbot Arena (Zheng et al. 2023) — discuss in Related Work as contamination-bypassing alternatives\n- Deeper DCR engagement: Oren et al. 2024 structural comparison\n- Burnell et al. 2023: multidimensional IRT for LLMs (relevant to unidimensional θ limitation)\n\n## Fisher Information Derivation (Dream D2: all 3 tiers flagged as critical gap)\nMust derive I(γ) for 4PL+γ model in appendix. Currently stated without proof.\nThe derivation must show: (1) relationship between signal AUC and γ recoverability, (2) approximation assumptions, (3) how measurement error factors in.\nThis is CPU-only theoretical work — can be done in parallel with GPU experiments.\n","numLines":119,"startLine":1,"totalLines":119}}}
